Output~2025-04-06 23:38:14.098976: [RequestOutput(request_id=72, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Name five influential figures in the history of artificial intelligence. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4076, 4330, 32549, 12678, 304, 279, 3925, 315, 21075, 11478, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are five influential figures in the history of artificial intelligence:\n\n1. **Alan Turing** (1912-1954): A British mathematician, computer scientist, and logician, Turing is widely considered the father of computer science and artificial intelligence. He proposed the Turing Test, a measure of a machine\'s ability to exhibit intelligent behavior equivalent to, or indistinguishable from, that of a human.\n2. **Marvin Minsky** (1927-2016): An American computer scientist and cognitive scientist, Minsky was a pioneer in the field of artificial intelligence. He developed the first neural network simulator, the SNARC (Stochastic Neural-Analog Reinforcement Calculator), and co-authored the book "Perceptrons," which introduced the concept of multi-layer neural networks.\n3. **John McCarthy** (1927-2011): An American computer scientist and cognitive scientist, McCarthy is known for coining the term "Artificial Intelligence" in 1956. He was a key figure in the development of Lisp, a programming language that is still widely used in AI research today.\n4. **Frank Rosenblatt** (1928-1971): An American computer scientist and psychologist, Rosenblatt developed the perceptron, a type of feedforward neural network that was one of the first AI systems capable of learning from data.\n5. **Ray Kurzweil** (1948-present): An American inventor, entrepreneur, and futurist, Kurzweil is known for his work on optical character recognition, speech recognition, and natural language processing. He is also a prominent futurist and author, having written several books on the future of humanity and artificial intelligence.\n\nThese individuals have all made significant contributions to the development of artificial intelligence, and their work continues to influence the field today.', token_ids=[8586, 527, 4330, 32549, 12678, 304, 279, 3925, 315, 21075, 11478, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 68724, 95530, 334, 320, 7529, 17, 12, 6280, 19, 1680, 362, 8013, 21651, 1122, 11, 6500, 28568, 11, 323, 12496, 1122, 11, 95530, 374, 13882, 6646, 279, 7126, 315, 6500, 8198, 323, 21075, 11478, 13, 1283, 11223, 279, 95530, 3475, 11, 264, 6767, 315, 264, 5780, 596, 5845, 311, 31324, 25530, 7865, 13890, 311, 11, 477, 1280, 89747, 481, 505, 11, 430, 315, 264, 3823, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 12331, 9799, 386, 52541, 334, 320, 5926, 22, 12, 679, 21, 1680, 1556, 3778, 6500, 28568, 323, 25702, 28568, 11, 386, 52541, 574, 264, 54047, 304, 279, 2115, 315, 21075, 11478, 13, 1283, 8040, 279, 1176, 30828, 4009, 42991, 11, 279, 18407, 47572, 320, 626, 67054, 61577, 59016, 32051, 47169, 11167, 37128, 705, 323, 1080, 96471, 279, 2363, 330, 3976, 346, 3589, 2439, 1359, 902, 11784, 279, 7434, 315, 7447, 48435, 30828, 14488, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 13379, 45040, 334, 320, 5926, 22, 12, 679, 16, 1680, 1556, 3778, 6500, 28568, 323, 25702, 28568, 11, 45040, 374, 3967, 369, 1080, 5859, 279, 4751, 330, 9470, 16895, 22107, 1, 304, 220, 6280, 21, 13, 1283, 574, 264, 1401, 7216, 304, 279, 4500, 315, 56075, 11, 264, 15840, 4221, 430, 374, 2103, 13882, 1511, 304, 15592, 3495, 3432, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 38426, 35120, 2067, 1617, 334, 320, 5926, 23, 12, 4468, 16, 1680, 1556, 3778, 6500, 28568, 323, 545