Output~2025-04-06 23:38:17.539674: [RequestOutput(request_id=73, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Compile a list of 5 online programming languages for kids. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 55567, 264, 1160, 315, 220, 20, 2930, 15840, 15823, 369, 6980, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here are 5 online programming languages that are suitable for kids:\n\n1. **Scratch**: Developed by MIT, Scratch is a visual programming language that uses blocks instead of text-based code. It's designed for kids aged 8-16 and is perfect for beginners. Kids can create their own games, animations, and stories using Scratch.\n2. **Code.org**: Code.org is a non-profit organization that offers a range of coding courses and activities for kids. Their programming language, Code.org, is designed for kids aged 4-18 and uses a block-based coding system.\n3. **CodeMonkey**: CodeMonkey is a coding platform that teaches kids programming concepts through games and puzzles. It's designed for kids aged 9-14 and uses a visual programming language called Monkey.\n4. **Hopscotch**: Hopscotch is a visual programming language that allows kids to create their own games and animations using a drag-and-drop interface. It's designed for kids aged 8-12 and is available on both desktop and mobile devices.\n5. **Daisy the Dinosaur**: Daisy the Dinosaur is a simple programming language that uses a visual interface to teach kids the basics of programming. It's designed for kids aged 6-12 and is a great introduction to programming concepts.\n\nThese online programming languages are all free, fun, and easy to use, making them perfect for kids who are just starting out with coding.", token_ids=[8586, 527, 220, 20, 2930, 15840, 15823, 430, 527, 14791, 369, 6980, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 66608, 759, 96618, 80110, 555, 15210, 11, 81074, 374, 264, 9302, 15840, 4221, 430, 5829, 10215, 4619, 315, 1495, 6108, 2082, 13, 1102, 596, 6319, 369, 6980, 20330, 220, 23, 12, 845, 323, 374, 4832, 369, 47950, 13, 23338, 649, 1893, 872, 1866, 3953, 11, 27145, 11, 323, 7493, 1701, 81074, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 2123, 2726, 96618, 6247, 2726, 374, 264, 2536, 28926, 7471, 430, 6209, 264, 2134, 315, 11058, 14307, 323, 7640, 369, 6980, 13, 11205, 15840, 4221, 11, 6247, 2726, 11, 374, 6319, 369, 6980, 20330, 220, 19, 12, 972, 323, 5829, 264, 2565, 6108, 11058, 1887, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 2123, 97938, 96618, 6247, 97938, 374, 264, 11058, 5452, 430, 33992, 6980, 15840, 19476, 1555, 3953, 323, 47623, 13, 1102, 596, 6319, 369, 6980, 20330, 220, 24, 12, 975, 323, 5829, 264, 9302, 15840, 4221, 2663, 58937, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 88373, 2445, 94707, 96618, 26634, 2445, 94707, 374, 264, 9302, 15840, 4221, 430, 6276, 6980, 311, 1893, 872, 1866, 3953, 323, 27145, 1701, 264, 11161, 9976, 62871, 3834, 13, 1102, 596, 6319, 369, 6980, 20330, 220, 23, 12, 717, 323, 374, 2561, 389, 2225, 17963, 323, 6505, 7766, 627, 20, 13, 3146, 35, 50156, 279, 423, 89247, 96618, 71264, 279, 423, 89247, 374, 264, 4382, 15840, 4221, 430, 5829, 264, 9302, 3834, 311, 4639, 6980, 279, 32874, 315, 15840, 13, 1102, 596, 6319, 369, 6980, 20330, 220, 21, 12, 717, 323, 374, 264, 2294, 17219, 311, 15840, 19476, 382, 9673, 2930, 15840, 15823, 527, 682, 1949, 11, 2523, 11, 323, 4228, 311, 1005, 11, 3339, 1124, 4832, 369, 6980, 889, 527, 1120, 6041, 704, 449, 11058, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_m