Output~2025-04-06 23:39:55.801122: [RequestOutput(request_id=111, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Generate a conversation between two people discussing the movie Narcos. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 20400, 264, 10652, 1990, 1403, 1274, 25394, 279, 5818, 79420, 437, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here's a conversation between two people discussing the movie Narcos:\n\n**Samantha:** Hey, have you seen Narcos?\n\n**Alex:** Yeah, I binge-watched the whole series over the weekend. What about you?\n\n**Samantha:** Same here! I couldn't stop watching. I'm still reeling from the ending.\n\n**Alex:** Right? I know, it was so intense. I felt like I was right there with Pablo Escobar and the Cali cartel.\n\n**Samantha:** Exactly! The way they portrayed the characters was so realistic. I felt like I was getting a glimpse into the real-life events.\n\n**Alex:** And the acting was phenomenal. Wagner Moura as Pablo Escobar was incredible. He really brought the character to life.\n\n**Samantha:** Totally agree. And Boyd Holbrook as Steve Murphy was great too. I loved how they showed the cat-and-mouse game between the DEA and the cartel.\n\n**Alex:** Yeah, it was like a chess match. The tension was palpable. And the way they used real-life events and figures was so impressive.\n\n**Samantha:** I know, it was like a history lesson and a thriller all rolled into one. Did you find yourself feeling sympathetic towards Pablo at all?\n\n**Alex:** Honestly, yeah. Despite all the terrible things he did, you could see why he was driven to do what he did. He was a product of his environment and circumstances.\n\n**Samantha:** Exactly. And that's what made the show so complex. It wasn't just a black-and-white portrayal of good vs. evil.\n\n**Alex:** Absolutely. It was a nuanced exploration of the human condition. And the music was amazing too. That soundtrack was so catchy!\n\n**Samantha:** (laughs) Yeah, I found myself humming the theme song for days after watching the show.\n\n**Alex:** (laughs) Same here! Okay, so what did you think of the finale? Did you see it coming?\n\n**Samantha:** Honestly, I was surprised. I didn't think they'd go that route with Pablo's character.\n\n**Alex:** Yeah, it was a bold move. But it was also really fitting. The show was always about the consequences of the characters' actions, and that was the ultimate consequence.\n\n**Samantha:** Exactly. Okay, well, I think we've talked enough about Narcos for now. But I'm definitely going to miss it.\n\n**Alex:** (laughs) Same here. But", token_ids=[8586, 596, 264, 10652, 1990, 1403, 1274, 25394, 279, 5818, 79420, 437, 1473, 334, 50, 13005, 23218, 68063, 28653, 11, 617, 499, 3970, 79420, 437, 1980, 334, 28487, 68063, 22335, 11, 358, 73922, 2695, 35344, 279, 4459, 4101, 927, 279, 9178, 13, 3639, 922, 499, 1980, 334, 50, 13005, 23218, 68063, 26823, 1618, 0, 358, 7846, 956, 3009, 10307, 13, 358, 2846, 2103, 312, 20659, 505, 279, 13696, 382, 334, 28487, 68063, 10291, 30, 358, 1440, 11, 433, 574, 779, 19428, 13, 358, 6612, 1093, 358, 574, 1314, 1070, 449, 53863, 15917, 32493, 323, 279, 3400, 72, 80740, 382, 334, 50, 13005, 23218, 68063, 69590, 0, 578, 1648, 814, 45877, 279, 5885, 574, 779, 26569, 13, 358, 6612, 1093, 358, 574, 3794, 264, 40942, 1139, 279, 1972, 26928, 4455, 382, 334, 28487, 68063, 1628, 279, 15718, 574, 57492, 13, 52475, 51648, 64, 439, 53863, 15917, 32493, 574, 15400, 13, 1283, 2216, 7263, 279, 3752, 311, 2324, 382, 334, 50, 13005, 2