Output~2025-04-06 23:40:21.245559: [RequestOutput(request_id=123, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write down the steps to solve a Rubik’s Cube ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 1523, 279, 7504, 311, 11886, 264, 13134, 1609, 753, 43692, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Solving a Rubik's Cube can be a challenging and rewarding puzzle. Here are the steps to solve a Rubik's Cube:\n\n**Step 1: White Cross**\n\n* Hold the cube in front of you with the white cross facing upwards.\n* Solve the white cross on the top surface by twisting the top layer only.\n* Focus on one white edge piece and twist the top layer until it is in its correct position.\n* Repeat this process until all four white edge pieces are in their correct positions.\n\n**Step 2: White Corners**\n\n* Once the white cross is solved, focus on solving the white corners.\n* Twist the middle and top layers to move the white corners to their correct positions.\n* Use the algorithms (step-by-step moves) below to solve each white corner:\n\t+ U-D-U-D (up-down-up-down)\n\t+ U-D-L-U-D-L-U (up-down-left-up-down-left-up)\n\t+ U-D-R-U-D-R-U (up-down-right-up-down-right-up)\n* Repeat this process until all four white corners are in their correct positions.\n\n**Step 3: Yellow Cross**\n\n* Hold the cube in front of you with the white cross facing upwards.\n* Solve the yellow cross on the middle layer by twisting the middle and bottom layers.\n* Focus on one yellow edge piece and twist the middle and bottom layers until it is in its correct position.\n* Repeat this process until all four yellow edge pieces are in their correct positions.\n\n**Step 4: Yellow Corners**\n\n* Once the yellow cross is solved, focus on solving the yellow corners.\n* Twist the middle and bottom layers to move the yellow corners to their correct positions.\n* Use the algorithms below to solve each yellow corner:\n\t+ D-L-D-L-D-L (down-left-down-left-down-left)\n\t+ D-R-D-R-D-R (down-right-down-right-down-right)\n\t+ D-U-D-U-D-U (down-up-down-up-down-up)\n* Repeat this process until all four yellow corners are in their correct positions.\n\n**Step 5: Orientation of Last Layer**\n\n* Hold the cube in front of you with the yellow cross facing upwards.\n* Twist the bottom layer to orient the last layer's colors to their correct positions.\n* Use the algorithms below to orient each piece:\n\t+ R-U-R-U-R-U (right-up-right-up-right-up)\n\t+ L-U-L-U-L-U (left-up-left-up-left-up)\n\t+ F-U-F-U-F-U (front-up-front", token_ids=[50, 20222, 264, 13134, 1609, 596, 43692, 649, 387, 264, 17436, 323, 42093, 25649, 13, 5810, 527, 279, 7504, 311, 11886, 264, 13134, 1609, 596, 43692, 1473, 334, 8468, 220, 16, 25, 5929, 11511, 57277, 9, 23588, 279, 24671, 304, 4156, 315, 499, 449, 279, 4251, 5425, 13176, 45054, 627, 9, 64384, 279, 4251, 5425, 389, 279, 1948, 7479, 555, 80654, 279, 1948, 6324, 1193, 627, 9, 26891, 389, 832, 4251, 6964, 6710, 323, 27744, 279, 1948, 6324, 3156, 433, 374, 304, 1202, 4495, 2361, 627, 9, 45901, 420, 1920, 3156, 682, 3116, 4251, 6964, 9863, 527, 304, 872, 4495, 10093, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 17, 25, 5929, 22036, 388, 57277, 9, 9843, 279, 4251, 5425, 374, 29056, 11, 5357, 389, 22581, 279, 4251, 24359, 627, 9, 74474, 279, 6278, 323, 1948, 13931, 311, 3351, 279, 4251, 24359, 311, 872, 4495, 10093, 627, 9, 5560, 279, 26249, 320, 9710, 14656, 30308, 11031, 8, 3770, 311, 11886, 1855, 4251, 9309, 512, 197, 10, 549, 9607, 35681, 9607, 320, 455, 15220, 5352, 15220, 340, 197, 10, 549, 96