Output~2025-04-06 23:43:18.473780: [RequestOutput(request_id=187, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Provide two tips to help people stay productive. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 40665, 1403, 10631, 311, 1520, 1274, 4822, 27331, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here are two tips to help people stay productive:\n\n**Tip 1: Prioritize Your Tasks**\n\nOne of the most effective ways to stay productive is to prioritize your tasks. Make a list of all the tasks you need to complete and then rank them in order of importance and urgency. Focus on completing the most critical tasks first, and then move on to less pressing ones. This will help you stay focused and ensure that you're making progress on the most important tasks.\n\n**Tip 2: Use the Pomodoro Technique**\n\nAnother technique that can help you stay productive is the Pomodoro Technique. This involves working in focused 25-minute increments, followed by a 5-minute break. After four cycles, take a longer break of 15-30 minutes. This technique can help you stay focused and avoid burnout by providing regular breaks and helping you maintain a sustainable work pace.", token_ids=[8586, 527, 1403, 10631, 311, 1520, 1274, 4822, 27331, 1473, 334, 16394, 220, 16, 25, 32499, 27406, 4718, 47571, 57277, 4054, 315, 279, 1455, 7524, 5627, 311, 4822, 27331, 374, 311, 63652, 701, 9256, 13, 7557, 264, 1160, 315, 682, 279, 9256, 499, 1205, 311, 4686, 323, 1243, 7222, 1124, 304, 2015, 315, 12939, 323, 54917,