Output~2025-04-06 23:43:46.578038: [RequestOutput(request_id=200, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Goal:\\nYour customers have lined up so that every second customer orders tea (2nd, 4th, 6th, 8th, ...). You list them up and hand out T-Shirts for every prime number tea customer.\\nGiven the total number of customers you had this day, how many T-Shirts did you hand out?\\n\\nExample: You have 4 customers:\\nCustomer 1 orders something\\nCustomer 2 orders tea (1 tea customer)\\nCustomer 3 orders something\\nCustomer 4 orders tea and gets a T-Shirt (2 tea customer --> prime number 2)\\nAnswer is 1\\n\\nInput:\\nLine 1 : An integer n for the numbers of customers you had. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 41047, 7338, 77, 7927, 6444, 617, 32393, 709, 779, 430, 1475, 2132, 6130, 10373, 15600, 320, 17, 303, 11, 220, 19, 339, 11, 220, 21, 339, 11, 220, 23, 339, 11, 2564, 570, 1472, 1160, 1124, 709, 323, 1450, 704, 350, 31361, 20242, 369, 1475, 10461, 1396, 15600, 6130, 7255, 77, 22818, 279, 2860, 1396, 315, 6444, 499, 1047, 420, 1938, 11, 1268, 1690, 350, 31361, 20242, 1550, 499, 1450, 704, 33720, 77, 1734, 13617, 25, 1472, 617, 220, 19, 6444, 7338, 77, 13084, 220, 16, 10373, 2555, 1734, 13084, 220, 17, 10373, 15600, 320, 16, 15600, 6130, 10929, 77, 13084, 220, 18, 10373, 2555, 1734, 13084, 220, 19, 10373, 15600, 323, 5334, 264, 350, 76954, 320, 17, 15600, 6130, 3929, 10461, 1396, 220, 17, 10929, 77, 16533, 374, 220, 16, 1734, 1734, 2566, 7338, 77, 2519, 220, 16, 551, 1556, 7698, 308, 369, 279, 5219, 315, 6444, 499, 1047, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='To solve this problem, we need to find the number of prime numbers that are less than or equal to the given number of customers. We can do this by iterating from 2 to the given number and checking if each number is prime. If it is, we increment the count of T-Shirts handed out.\n\nHere is the Python code to solve this problem:\n\n```\ndef is_prime(num):\n    if num < 2:\n        return False\n    for i in range(2, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n        if num % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\nn = int(input())\nt_shirts = 0\nfor i in range(2, n+1, 2):\n    if is_prime(i):\n        t_shirts += 1\nprint(t_shirts)\n```\n\nYou can run this code and input the number of customers to get the number of T-Shirts handed out.', token_ids=[1271, 11886, 420, 3575, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1505, 279, 1396, 315, 10461, 5219, 430, 527, 2753, 1109, 477, 6273, 311, 279, 2728, 1396, 315, 6444, 13, 1226, 649, 656, 420, 555, 88335, 505, 220, 17, 311, 279, 2728, 1396, 323, 13598, 422, 1855, 1396, 374, 10461, 13, 1442, 433, 374, 11, 584, 16650, 279, 1797, 315, 350, 31361, 20242, 23415, 704, 382, 8586, 374, 279, 13325, 2082, 311, 11886, 420, 3575, 1473, 14196, 4077, 755, 374, 39317, 8228, 997, 262, 422, 1661, 366, 220, 17, 512, 286, 471, 3641, 198, 262, 369, 602, 304, 2134, 7, 17, 11, 528, 8228, 334, 15, 13, 20, 8, 489, 220, 16, 997, 286, 422, 1661, 1034, 602, 624, 220, 15, 512, 310, 471, 3641, 198, 262, 471, 3082, 271, 77, 284, 528, 5498, 2455, 83, 3797, 20242, 284, 220, 15, 198, 2000, 602, 304, 2134, 7, 17, 11, 308, 10, 16, 11, 220, 17, 997, 262, 422, 374, 39317, 1998, 997, 286, 259, 3797, 20242, 1447, 220, 16, 198, 1374, 1175, 3797, 20242, 340, 14196, 19884, 2675, 649, 1629, 420, 2082, 323, 1988, 279, 1396, 315, 6444, 311, 636, 279, 1396, 315, 350, 31361, 20242, 23415, 704, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished