Output~2025-04-06 23:44:07.473685: [RequestOutput(request_id=211, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Provide an example of effective body language when giving a presentation. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 40665, 459, 3187, 315, 7524, 2547, 4221, 994, 7231, 264, 15864, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here's an example of effective body language when giving a presentation:\n\n**Maintaining Eye Contact**: When presenting, it's essential to make eye contact with your audience. This helps to build trust, establish a connection, and convey confidence. Aim to maintain eye contact with different people in the room for about 2-3 seconds at a time, scanning the room to engage with everyone. Avoid staring at one person for too long, as this can make others feel left out.\n\n**Confident Posture**: Stand up straight and maintain good posture while presenting. This conveys confidence and authority. Keep your shoulders back, chest open, and weight evenly distributed on both feet. Avoid leaning forward or backward, as this can make you appear uncertain or defensive.\n\n**Hand Gestures**: Use hand gestures to emphasize key points and add variety to your presentation. Keep your hands relaxed and avoid fidgeting or crossing your arms, which can give the impression that you're closed off or defensive. Use open and expansive gestures, such as sweeping your arms or pointing to a diagram, to engage your audience.\n\n**Facial Expressions**: Use facial expressions to convey enthusiasm and passion for your topic. Smile when sharing interesting or important points, and avoid looking bored or disinterested. A genuine smile can help to build rapport with your audience and make your presentation more engaging.\n\n**Proximity**: Vary your proximity to the audience to keep them engaged. Move around the room or use the space to emphasize key points or illustrate a concept. Avoid standing too close to the audience, as this can be overwhelming, or too far away, which can make you appear distant or unengaged.\n\n**Avoiding Fidgeting**: Avoid fidgeting with your hands, pen, or other objects while presenting. This can give the impression that you're nervous or distracted. Keep your hands still and focused on your presentation, using them to emphasize key points or illustrate a concept.\n\nBy incorporating these effective body language techniques into your presentation, you can engage your audience, convey confidence and authority, and deliver a more impactful and memorable presentation.", token_ids=[8586, 596, 459, 3187, 315, 7524, 2547, 4221, 994, 7231, 264, 15864, 1473, 334, 67834, 2101, 28929, 9359, 96618, 3277, 32644, 11, 433, 596, 7718, 311, 1304, 8071, 3729, 449, 701, 10877, 13, 1115, 8779, 311, 1977, 7095, 11, 5813, 264, 3717, 11, 323, 20599, 12410, 13, 71715, 311, 10519, 8071, 3729, 449, 2204, 1274, 304, 279, 3130, 369, 922, 220, 17, 12, 18, 6622, 520, 264, 892, 11, 36201, 279, 3130, 311, 16988, 449, 5127, 13, 35106, 37874, 520, 832, 1732, 369, 2288, 1317, 11, 439, 420, 649, 1304, 3885, 2733, 2163, 704, 382, 334, 15949, 1748, 3962, 554, 96618, 15948, 709, 7833, 323, 10519, 1695, 48378, 1418, 32644, 13, 1115, 390, 50369, 12410, 323, 11447, 13, 13969, 701, 28004, 1203, 11, 15489, 1825, 11, 323, 4785, 42147, 4332, 389, 2225, 7693, 13, 35106, 49448, 4741, 477, 28655, 11, 439, 420, 649, 1304, 499, 5101, 36218, 477, 16399, 382, 334, 2367, 54999, 1439, 96618, 5560, 1450, 53492, 311, 47032, 1401, 3585, 323, 923, 8205, 311, 701, 15864, 