Output~2025-04-06 23:46:19.464809: [RequestOutput(request_id=266, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the behavior of a rock falling through air. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 7865, 315, 264, 7091, 16054, 1555, 3805, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='When a rock falls through the air, it exhibits a predictable and fascinating behavior. Initially, the rock begins to accelerate downward due to the force of gravity, which is the combined effect of the Earth\'s mass and the rock\'s mass. As the rock falls, it experiences an upward force opposing its motion, known as air resistance or drag. This force is caused by the interaction between the rock\'s surface and the air molecules it encounters.\n\nAs the rock falls, the air resistance increases as the rock\'s velocity increases. This is because the air molecules are pushed out of the way by the rock\'s motion, creating a "wake" behind it. The air molecules then rush back to fill the space, creating a region of higher air pressure above the rock and a region of lower air pressure below it. This pressure difference creates an upward force on the rock, opposing its downward motion.\n\nThe combination of gravity and air resistance causes the rock to accelerate downward at a decreasing rate. The rock\'s velocity increases rapidly at first, but as air resistance increases, the acceleration slows down. Eventually, the rock reaches its terminal velocity, which is the maximum velocity it can achieve while falling through the air. At this point, the force of gravity is balanced by the force of air resistance, and the rock falls at a constant velocity.\n\nAs the rock continues to fall, it will eventually reach the ground, where it will come to rest. The distance it travels before hitting the ground depends on its initial height, its terminal velocity, and the air density. The rock\'s behavior during its fall is influenced by factors such as its shape, size, and surface texture, which can affect the amount of air resistance it encounters.', token_ids=[4599, 264, 7091, 17503, 1555, 279, 3805, 11, 433, 50829, 264, 45207, 323, 27387, 7865, 13, 59656, 11, 279, 7091, 12302, 311, 43880, 45578, 4245, 311, 279, 5457, 315, 24128, 11, 902, 374, 279, 11093, 2515, 315, 279, 9420, 596, 3148, 323, 279, 7091, 596, 3148, 13, 1666, 279, 7091, 17503, 11, 433, 11704, 459, 40872, 5457, 31322, 1202, 11633, 11, 3967, 439, 3805, 13957, 477, 11161, 13, 1115, 5457, 374, 9057, 555, 279, 16628, 1990, 279, 7091, 596, 7479, 323, 279, 3805, 35715, 433, 35006, 382, 2170, 279, 7091, 17503, 11, 279, 3805, 13957, 12992, 439, 279, 7091, 596, 15798, 12992, 13, 1115, 374, 1606, 279, 3805, 35715, 527, 15753, 704, 315, 279, 1648, 555, 279, 7091, 596, 11633, 11, 6968, 264, 330, 91019, 1, 4920, 433, 13, 578, 3805, 35715, 1243, 13270, 1203, 311, 5266, 279, 3634, 11, 6968, 264, 5654, 315, 5190, 3805, 7410, 3485, 279, 7091, 323, 264, 5654, 315, 4827, 3805, 7410, 3770, 433, 13, 1115, 7410, 6811, 11705, 459, 40872, 5457, 389, 279, 7091, 11, 31322, 1202, 45578, 11633, 382, 791, 10824, 315, 24128, 323, 3805, 13957, 11384, 279, 7091, 311, 43880, 45578, 520, 264, 44649, 4478, 13, 578, 7091, 596, 15798, 12992, 19019, 520, 1176, 11, 719, 439, 3805, 13957, 12992, 11, 279, 31903, 70270, 1523, 13, 38274, 11, 279, 7091, 25501, 1202, 15372, 15798, 11, 902, 374, 279, 7340, 15798, 433, 649, 11322, 1418, 16054, 1555, 279, 3805, 13, 2468, 420, 1486, 11, 279, 5457, 315, 24128, 374, 24770, 555, 279, 5457, 315, 3805, 13957, 11, 323, 279, 7091, 17503, 520, 264, 6926, 15798, 382, 2170, 279, 7091, 9731, 311, 4498, 11, 433, 690, 9778, 5662, 279, 5015, 11, 1405, 433, 690, 2586, 311, 2800, 13, 578, 6138, 433, 35292, 1603, 20129, 279, 5015, 14117, 389, 1202, 2926, 2673, 11, 1202, 15372, 15798, 11, 323, 279, 3805, 17915, 13, 578, 7091, 596, 7865, 2391, 1202, 4498, 374, 28160, 555, 9547, 1778, 439, 1202, 6211, 11, 1404, 11, 323, 7479, 10651, 11, 902, 649, 7958, 279, 3392, 315, 3805, 13957, 433, 35006, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
