Output~2025-04-06 23:47:17.562092: [RequestOutput(request_id=286, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: List three differences between the two given terms ### Input: Open Source Software and Proprietary Software ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 1796, 2380, 12062, 1990, 279, 1403, 2728, 3878, 17010, 5688, 25, 5377, 8922, 4476, 323, 3998, 462, 16238, 4476, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are three differences between Open Source Software and Proprietary Software:\n\n**1. Ownership and Control**: Open Source Software is owned and controlled by the community of developers who contribute to it, whereas Proprietary Software is owned and controlled by a single company or individual. This means that Open Source Software is often developed collaboratively and transparently, while Proprietary Software is developed and controlled by a single entity.\n\n**2. Licensing**: Open Source Software is typically licensed under a license that allows users to modify, distribute, and use the software freely, as long as they comply with the terms of the license. Proprietary Software, on the other hand, is licensed under a proprietary license that restricts the use and distribution of the software, often requiring users to pay royalties or fees.\n\n**3. Cost**: Open Source Software is often free or low-cost, as the development and maintenance costs are covered by the community of users and contributors. Proprietary Software, on the other hand, is often expensive, as the development and maintenance costs are covered by the company or individual that owns the software.\n\nThese differences reflect the fundamental philosophies and approaches of Open Source and Proprietary Software development, with Open Source emphasizing collaboration, transparency, and community involvement, and Proprietary Software emphasizing control, secrecy, and profit.', token_ids=[8586, 527, 2380, 12062, 1990, 5377, 8922, 4476, 323, 3998, 462, 16238, 4476, 1473, 334, 16, 13, 86036, 323, 7935, 96618, 5377, 8922, 4476, 374, 13234, 323, 14400, 555, 279, 4029, 315, 13707, 889, 17210, 311, 433, 11, 20444, 3998, 462, 16238, 4476, 374, 13234, 323, 14400, 555, 264, 3254, 2883, 477, 3927, 13, 1115, 3445, 430, 5377, 8922, 4476, 374, 3629, 8040, 11430, 8046, 323, 18300, 398, 11, 1418, 3998, 462, 16238, 4476, 374, 8040, 323, 14400, 555, 264, 3254, 5502, 382, 334, 17, 13, 73425, 96618, 5377, 8922, 4476, 374, 11383, 16383, 1234, 264, 5842, 430, 6276, 3932, 311, 5719, 11, 16822, 11, 323, 1005, 279, 3241, 26662, 11, 439, 1317, 439, 814, 26069, 449, 279, 3878, 315, 279, 5842, 13, 3998, 462, 16238, 4476, 11, 389, 279, 1023, 1450, 11, 374, 16383, 1234, 264, 34333, 5842, 430, 9067, 82, 279, 1005, 323, 8141, 315, 279, 3241, 11, 3629, 23537, 3932, 311, 2343, 85974, 477, 12718, 382, 334, 18, 13, 11443, 96618, 5377, 8922, 4476, 374, 3629, 1949, 477, 3428, 41238, 11, 439, 279, 4500, 323, 13709, 7194, 527, 9960, 555, 279, 4029, 315, 3932, 323, 20965, 13, 3998, 462, 16238, 4476, 11, 389, 279, 1023, 1450, 11, 374, 3629, 11646, 11, 439, 279, 4500, 323, 13709, 7194, 527, 9960, 555, 279, 2883, 477, 3927, 430, 25241, 279, 3241, 382, 9673, 12062, 8881, 279, 16188, 13868, 552, 323, 20414, 315, 5377, 8922, 323, 3998, 462, 16238, 4476, 4500, 11, 449, 5377, 8922, 82003, 20632, 11, 28330, 11, 323, 4029, 22315, 11, 323, 3998, 462, 16238, 4476, 82003, 2585, 11, 61059, 11, 323, 11626, 13, 128009]