{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Goal:\nLet there be a right triangle with sides a, b and c, where c is the hypotenuse. h is the height drawn from the right angle to c and splits the hypotenuse to ca (segment connected to the side a) and cb (segment connected to the side b).\nAs Euclid stated, when given the hypotenuse length c and the length of one of the hypotenuse segments cb, it is possible to determine the length of all sides and of the height, by using this formula:\nh² = ca * cb\n\nBy using this formula and/or any other formulas of your choice, calculate the length of the two remaining sides (a and b) and the height (h) of the triangle.\n\nIn the event of wrong data found in the input, print the word INCORRECT.\n\nAll the outputs will need to be truncated to 2 decimal places.\n\nInput:\nSpace separated string containing 2 positive integers describing the lengths of the side c c and the segment cb cb , or strings whenever wrong data is present.\n\nOutput:\nthe lengths of side a a, side b b and height h h, separated by spaces, or INCORRECT if wrong data is present. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>



