7, 3160, 272, 323, 279, 3160, 315, 832, 315, 279, 9950, 66728, 817, 21282, 10059, 11, 433, 374, 3284, 311, 8417, 279, 3160, 315, 682, 11314, 323, 315, 279, 2673, 11, 555, 1701, 420, 15150, 7338, 17134, 30556, 284, 2211, 353, 10059, 1734, 1734, 1383, 1701, 420, 15150, 323, 5255, 904, 1023, 55179, 315, 701, 5873, 11, 11294, 279, 3160, 315, 279, 1403, 9861, 11314, 320, 64, 323, 293, 8, 323, 279, 2673, 320, 71, 8, 315, 279, 22217, 7255, 77, 1734, 644, 279, 1567, 315, 5076, 828, 1766, 304, 279, 1988, 11, 1194, 279, 3492, 18610, 878, 45940, 7255, 77, 1734, 2460, 279, 16674, 690, 1205, 311, 387, 60856, 311, 220, 17, 12395, 7634, 7255, 77, 1734, 2566, 7338, 77, 10115, 19180, 925, 8649, 220, 17, 6928, 26864, 23524, 279, 29416, 315, 279, 3185, 272, 272, 323, 279, 10449, 10059, 10059, 1174, 477, 9246, 15716, 5076, 828, 374, 3118, 7255, 77, 1734, 5207, 7338, 77, 1820, 29416, 315, 3185, 264, 264, 11, 3185, 293, 293, 323, 2673, 305, 305, 11, 19180, 555, 12908, 11, 477, 18610, 878, 45940, 422, 5076, 828, 374, 3118, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a Python solution for the problem:\n\n```python\ndef calculate_triangle_sides(c, cb):\n    if not (isinstance(c, int) and isinstance(cb, int)):\n        return \'INCORRECT\'\n    if c <= 0 or cb <= 0:\n        return \'INCORRECT\'\n    h = (cb * c) ** 0.5\n    a = (c ** 2 - cb ** 2) ** 0.5\n    b = c - a\n    return f"{a:.2f} {b:.2f} {h:.2f}"\n\nc, cb = map(int, input().split())\nprint(calculate_triangle_sides(c, cb))\n```\n\nThis program first checks if the input values are integers and positive. If not, it returns \'INCORRECT\'. Then it calculates the height using the formula `h² = ca * cb`, and then calculates the lengths of sides a and b using the Pythagorean theorem and the fact that `b = c - a`. The results are then printed with two decimal places.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 133