Output~2025-04-06 23:50:06.644550: [RequestOutput(request_id=339, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Please generate a to do list for writing a 10 page research paper. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 5321, 7068, 264, 311, 656, 1160, 369, 4477, 264, 220, 605, 2199, 3495, 5684, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a suggested to-do list for writing a 10-page research paper:\n\n**Week 1-2: Research and Planning**\n\n1. **Choose a topic**: Select a topic that interests you and is relevant to the course or field of study.\n2. **Conduct preliminary research**: Read and gather information from various sources (books, articles, online resources) to get a general understanding of the topic.\n3. **Develop a research question**: Formulate a specific research question or hypothesis to guide your investigation.\n4. **Create an outline**: Organize your thoughts and structure your paper with a detailed outline, including introduction, literature review, methodology, results, discussion, and conclusion.\n5. **Develop a thesis statement**: Write a clear and concise thesis statement that summarizes the main argument or finding of your paper.\n\n**Week 3-4: Literature Review and Research**\n\n1. **Conduct in-depth research**: Gather and analyze relevant literature, including academic articles, books, and online resources.\n2. **Take notes and organize sources**: Record important information, quotes, and insights from your research, and organize them by theme or category.\n3. **Analyze and synthesize information**: Evaluate the credibility and relevance of sources, and identify patterns, contradictions, and gaps in the literature.\n4. **Identify key findings and arguments**: Determine the main findings and arguments that will support your thesis statement.\n\n**Week 5-6: Writing and Drafting**\n\n1. **Write the introduction**: Introduce the topic, provide background information, and include a thesis statement.\n2. **Write the literature review**: Summarize and analyze the key findings and arguments from your research.\n3. **Write the methodology**: Describe the research design, methods, and procedures used to collect and analyze data.\n4. **Write the results**: Present the findings of your research, including any data, statistics, or visual aids.\n5. **Write the discussion**: Interpret the results, relate them to the literature, and discuss the implications and limitations of your research.\n\n**Week 7-8: Revising and Editing**\n\n1. **Revise the draft**: Review and revise the paper, ensuring that it is well-organized, clear, and concise.\n2. **Edit for grammar and punctuation**: Check for errors in grammar, punctuation, and spelling.\n3. **Get feedback from peers or mentors**: Share your draft with others and incorporate their feedback and suggestions.\n4. **Finalize the paper**: Make any final revisions and proofread the', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 12090, 311, 30659, 1160, 369, 4477, 264, 220, 605, 15463, 3495, 5684, 1473, 334, 17490, 220, 16, 12, 17, 25, 8483, 323, 28780, 57277, 16, 13, 3146, 25017, 264, 8712, 96618, 8593, 264, 8712, 430, 12034, 499, 323, 374, 9959, 311, 279, 3388, 477, 2115, 315, 4007, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 1128, 1076, 33269, 3495, 96618, 4557, 323, 9762, 2038, 505, 5370, 8336, 320, 12383, 11, 9908, 11, 2930, 5070, 8, 311, 636, 264, 4689, 8830, 315, 279, 8712, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 21076, 264, 3495, 3488, 96618, 3459, 6468, 264, 3230, 3495, 3488, 477, 31178, 311, 8641, 701, 8990, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 41