Output~2025-04-06 23:53:13.236008: [RequestOutput(request_id=410, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: How can I make a classic Manhattan cocktail? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 2650, 649, 358, 1304, 264, 11670, 29890, 41010, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The classic Manhattan! A timeless and sophisticated cocktail that's easy to make and always a crowd-pleaser. Here's a step-by-step guide to crafting the perfect Manhattan:\n\nIngredients:\n\n* 2 oz (60 ml) whiskey (bourbon or rye work well)\n* 1 oz (30 ml) sweet vermouth\n* 2 dashes Angostura bitters\n* Cherry garnish (optional, but highly recommended)\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. Fill a mixing glass with ice. Yes, you read that right - a mixing glass, not a shaker! This will help prevent the drink from getting watered down.\n2. Pour the whiskey, vermouth, and bitters over the ice.\n3. Stir the mixture for about 30-45 seconds to chill and dilute the ingredients. You want to aim for a temperature around 45°F (7°C) to 50°F (10°C).\n4. Strain the mixture into a chilled coupe or cocktail glass. You can use a Hawthorne strainer or a julep strainer to prevent any ice or sediment from entering the glass.\n5. Garnish with a cherry, if desired. A maraschino cherry is traditional, but you can also use a Luxardo cherry or a homemade cherry syrup for a more nuanced flavor.\n6. Serve and enjoy!\n\nTips and Variations:\n\n* Use a good quality whiskey: The type of whiskey you choose will greatly impact the flavor of your Manhattan. Bourbon and rye are classic choices, but you can also experiment with other types like Canadian whiskey or blended whiskey.\n* Adjust the ratio: Some people prefer a 3:1 or 4:1 whiskey-to-vermouth ratio. Feel free to experiment and find your perfect balance.\n* Try different bitters: While Angostura bitters are traditional, you can also experiment with other types of bitters, like orange or chocolate bitters, to add unique flavor profiles.\n* Experiment with sweet vermouth: There are many types of sweet vermouth out there, from Carpano Antica to Dolin. Find one that you like and use it to make your Manhattan.\n\nNow, go ahead and shake (or rather, stir) things up with this classic cocktail!", token_ids=[791, 11670, 29890, 0, 362, 58105, 323, 27877, 41010, 430, 596, 4228, 311, 1304, 323, 2744, 264, 13734, 12, 698, 12351, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 3094, 14656, 30308, 8641, 311, 45167, 279, 4832, 29890, 1473, 46847, 1473, 9, 220, 17, 25616, 320, 1399, 16116, 8, 65354, 320, 15747, 6098, 477, 436, 9188, 990, 1664, 340, 9, 220, 16, 25616, 320, 966, 16116, 8, 10437, 2807, 33780, 198, 9, 220, 17, 88646, 7568, 537, 5808, 293, 29163, 198, 9, 45805, 61016, 819, 320, 13099, 11, 719, 7701, 11349, 696, 56391, 1473, 16, 13, 22748, 264, 27890, 9168, 449, 10054, 13, 7566, 11, 499, 1373, 430, 1314, 482, 264, 27890, 9168, 11, 539, 264, 559, 4506, 0, 1115, 690, 1520, 5471, 279, 7172, 505, 3794, 3090, 291, 1523, 627, 17, 13, 27058, 279, 65354, 11, 2807, 33780, 11, 323, 293, 29163, 927, 279, 10054, 627, 18, 13, 65292, 279, 21655, 369, 922, 220, 966, 12, 1774, 6622, 311, 37401, 323, 19371, 1088, 279, 14293, 13, 1472, 1390, 311, 9395, 369, 264, 9499, 2212, 220, 1774, 59572, 320, 22, 32037, 8, 311, 220, 1135, 59572, 320, 605, 32037, 4390, 19, 13, 4610, 467, 279, 21655, 1139, 264, 85042, 88609, 477, 41010, 9168, 13, 1472, 649, 1005, 264, 86883, 17334, 610, 1780, 477, 264, 503, 1130, 79, 610, 1780, 311, 5471, 904, 10054, 477, 59132, 505, 16661, 279, 9168, 627, 20, 13, 6513