Output~2025-04-06 23:53:47.276435: [RequestOutput(request_id=416, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: How can I keep my house cool in the heat? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 2650, 649, 358, 2567, 856, 3838, 7155, 304, 279, 8798, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here's a response that provides some helpful tips on how to keep your house cool in the heat:\n\n**Keep Your House Cool in the Heat: 10 Effective Tips**\n\nSummer heat can be unbearable, making it essential to find ways to keep your house cool and comfortable. Here are 10 effective tips to help you beat the heat:\n\n1. **Use Natural Ventilation**: Open windows and doors to allow cool air to enter your home, especially during the early morning or evening when the outside temperature is cooler. Use fans to circulate the air and keep it moving.\n2. **Use Shades and Blinds**: Close curtains, blinds, and shades during the hottest part of the day (usually between 11 am and 3 pm) to block out direct sunlight, which can heat up your home.\n3. **Upgrade to Energy-Efficient Windows**: Consider replacing old windows with energy-efficient, double-glazed windows that can help keep the heat out and the cool air in.\n4. **Use Ceiling Fans**: Ceiling fans can circulate air and make your home feel cooler, allowing you to raise your thermostat by 2-3°F without feeling the difference.\n5. **Keep Your Home Well-Maintained**: Regularly clean your air conditioning unit, change air filters, and ensure your home's insulation is in good condition to prevent heat from seeping in.\n6. **Use a Programmable Thermostat**: Install a programmable thermostat to regulate your home's temperature, so it's cooler when you're home and warmer when you're away.\n7. **Use Cool Colors**: Paint your roof and exterior walls with cool colors, such as light gray or beige, to reflect the sun's rays and keep your home cooler.\n8. **Plant Trees and Greenery**: Strategically plant trees and greenery around your home to provide shade and block direct sunlight.\n9. **Use a Dehumidifier**: High humidity can make your home feel hotter than it actually is. Use a dehumidifier to remove excess moisture from the air and make your home feel cooler.\n10. **Stay Hydrated**: Finally, don't forget to stay hydrated by drinking plenty of water and taking cool showers or baths to help your body regulate its temperature.\n\nBy following these simple tips, you can keep your house cool and comfortable even during the hottest summer months.", token_ids=[8586, 596, 264, 2077, 430, 5825, 1063, 11190, 10631, 389, 1268, 311, 2567, 701, 3838, 7155, 304, 279, 8798, 1473, 334, 19999, 4718, 4783, 24882, 304, 279, 27162, 25, 220, 605, 48023, 26788, 57277, 51787, 8798, 649, 387, 99930, 11, 3339, 433, 7718, 311, 1505, 5627, 311, 2567, 701, 3838, 7155, 323, 10882, 13, 5810, 527, 220, 605, 7524, 10631, 311, 1520, 499, 9567, 279, 8798, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 10464, 18955, 27505, 13763, 96618, 5377, 11276, 323, 14365, 311, 2187, 7155, 3805, 311, 3810, 701, 2162, 11, 5423, 2391, 279, 4216, 6693, 477, 11714, 994, 279, 4994, 9499, 374, 36921, 13, 5560, 7359, 311, 4319, 6468, 279, 3805, 323, 2567, 433, 7366, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 10464, 81247, 323, 2563, 8843, 96618, 13330, 54499, 11, 67161, 11, 323, 37199, 2391, 279, 38391, 961, 315, 279, 1938, 320, 44066, 1990, 220, 806, 1097, 323, 220, 18, 9012, 8, 311, 2565, 704, 2167, 40120, 11, 902, 649, 8798, 709, 701, 2162, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 44961, 311, 12634, 13737, 544, 5499, 5632, 96618, 218