Output~2025-04-06 23:58:20.446041: [RequestOutput(request_id=530, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Create a list of books that would be appropriate for a 5th grade student to read. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4324, 264, 1160, 315, 6603, 430, 1053, 387, 8475, 369, 264, 220, 20, 339, 12239, 5575, 311, 1373, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here\'s a list of books that are suitable for a 5th grade student to read:\n\n**Classic Favorites**\n\n1. "Charlotte\'s Web" by E.B. White - A timeless tale of friendship and loyalty between a pig and a spider.\n2. "The Tale of Despereaux" by Kate DiCamillo - A charming story about a brave and book-loving mouse on a quest to save a princess.\n3. "The Secret Garden" by Frances Hodgson Burnett - A classic coming-of-age story about a spoiled girl who discovers a hidden garden and, through her care of it, learns about friendship and herself.\n\n**Adventure and Fantasy**\n\n1. "The Magic Tree House" series by Mary Pope Osborne - A series of books that follow two siblings as they travel through time and around the world, exploring different cultures and historical events.\n2. "The Lemonade War" by Jacqueline Davies - A fun and humorous story about two siblings who start a lemonade stand and learn valuable lessons about business, family, and friendship.\n3. "The Beyonders" series by Brandon Mull - A high-fantasy series about a boy who discovers a secret world of magic and monsters.\n\n**Realistic Fiction**\n\n1. "Wonder" by R.J. Palacio - A heartwarming story about a boy with a rare facial deformity and his journey to find acceptance and friendship.\n2. "The Giver" by Lois Lowry - A dystopian novel that explores themes of identity, memory, and the importance of human emotions.\n3. "Bridge to Terabithia" by Katherine Paterson - A poignant story about two friends who find solace in their imagination and each other.\n\n**Humor and Mystery**\n\n1. "Captain Underpants" series by Dav Pilkey - A hilarious and action-packed series about two mischievous fourth-graders who accidentally create a superhero.\n2. "The Westing Game" by Ellen Raskin - A clever mystery novel about a group of strangers who are brought together to solve a puzzle and uncover a hidden treasure.\n3. "Frindle" by Andrew Clements - A lighthearted story about a boy who invents a new word and explores the power of language and creativity.\n\nThese books offer a mix of adventure, humor, and heart, and are sure to engage and entertain a 5th grade student.', token_ids=[8586, 596, 264, 1160, 315, 6603, 430, 527, 14791, 369, 264, 220, 20, 339, 12239, 5575, 311, 1373, 1473, 334, 64431, 64318, 57277, 16, 13, 330, 96995, 596, 5000, 1, 555, 469, 1823, 13, 5929, 482, 362, 58105, 24162, 315, 27607, 323, 32883, 1990, 264, 24623, 323, 264, 35454, 627, 17, 13, 330, 791, 55448, 315, 3959, 79, 486, 12249, 1, 555, 30301, 7923, 34, 21606, 385, 482, 362, 35509, 3446, 922, 264, 34300, 323, 2363, 77700, 8814, 389, 264, 2271, 311, 3665, 264, 40688, 627, 18, 13, 330, 791, 8769, 19558, 1, 555, 43833, 83984, 942, 99994, 482, 362, 11670, 5108, 8838, 44041, 3446, 922, 264, 72524, 3828, 889, 52114, 264, 8340, 13863, 323, 11, 1555, 1077, 2512, 315, 433, 11, 47310, 922, 27607, 323, 11937, 382, 334, 90198, 323, 27582, 57277, 16, 13, 330, 791, 15852, 9119, 4783, 1, 4101, 555, 10455, 30460, 71229, 482, 362, 4101, 315, 6603, 430, 1833, 1403, 37783, 439, 814, 5944, 1555, 892, 323, 2212, 279, 1917, 11, 24919, 2204, 27833, 323, 13970, 4455, 627, 1