n and implement a new feature or module in a software application?\n3. Can you walk me through your thought process when approaching a new problem or challenge?\n4. How do you prioritize and manage multiple tasks and projects simultaneously?\n5. Can you describe your experience with Agile development methodologies, such as Scrum or Kanban?\n\n**Collaboration and Communication**\n\n1. Can you give an example of a time when you had to work with a difficult team member or customer, and how you handled the situation?\n2. How do you communicate technical information to non-technical stakeholders, such as project managers or customers?\n3. Can you describe your experience with version control systems, such as Git?\n4. How do you handle conflicting opinions or disagreements with colleagues during a project?\n5. Can you walk me through your experience with pair programming or code reviews?\n\n**Behavioral Questions**\n\n1. Can you tell me about a time when you had to adapt to a new technology or framework quickly?\n2. How do you handle tight deadlines and high-pressure situations?\n3. Can you describe a project you worked on that you're particularly proud of, and what your role was in it?\n4. How do you prioritize your own professional development and continuous learning?\n5. Can you tell me about a time when you received feedback or criticism on your code or work, and how you responded to it?\n\n**Scenario-Based Questions", token_ids=[8586, 527, 1063, 4279, 7274, 4860, 430, 649, 387, 1511, 311, 8720, 264, 9322, 596, 7512, 323, 3217, 369, 264, 3241, 4500, 3560, 1473, 334, 38255, 323, 25837, 57277, 16, 13, 3053, 499, 3371, 757, 264, 2697, 922, 701, 4092, 323, 1268, 499, 2751, 1139, 3241, 4500, 5380, 17, 13, 3639, 12521, 988, 499, 311, 990, 304, 3241, 4500, 11, 323, 1148, 656, 499, 4774, 1455, 922, 433, 5380, 18, 13, 3053, 499, 4321, 757, 1555, 701, 6873, 323, 9959, 82571, 1980, 334, 63326, 31340, 57277, 16, 13, 3639, 15840, 15823, 527, 499, 69365, 304, 11, 323, 649, 499, 304