Output~2025-04-07 00:00:36.402456: [RequestOutput(request_id=574, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: List four characteristics of a democratic system. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 1796, 3116, 17910, 315, 264, 26623, 1887, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are four characteristics of a democratic system:\n\n1. **Representative Government**: In a democratic system, citizens elect representatives to make decisions on their behalf. These representatives are accountable to the people and are expected to act in their best interests.\n2. **Free and Fair Elections**: Democratic systems hold regular, free, and fair elections where citizens can choose their leaders and representatives. This ensures that power is transferred peacefully and that the will of the people is reflected in the government.\n3. **Protection of Individual Rights**: Democratic systems prioritize the protection of individual rights and freedoms, such as freedom of speech, assembly, and religion. This ensures that citizens are able to participate in the political process and express their opinions without fear of persecution.\n4. **Separation of Powers**: Democratic systems often have a system of checks and balances, where power is divided among different branches of government (e.g. executive, legislative, and judicial). This prevents any one branch from becoming too powerful and ensures that decisions are made in a way that is fair and accountable.', token_ids=[8586, 527,