Output~2025-04-07 00:01:17.364970: [RequestOutput(request_id=585, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: A proposal will make years that end in double zeroes a leap year only if the year leaves a remainder of 200 or 600 when divided by 900. Under this proposal, how many leap years will there be that end in double zeroes between 1996 and 4096? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 362, 14050, 690, 1304, 1667, 430, 842, 304, 2033, 98543, 264, 32571, 1060, 1193, 422, 279, 1060, 11141, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 1049, 477, 220, 5067, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 13, 9636, 420, 14050, 11, 1268, 1690, 32571, 1667, 690, 1070, 387, 430, 842, 304, 2033, 98543, 1990, 220, 2550, 21, 323, 220, 12378, 21, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Let's analyze the proposal:\n\n* A year ends in double zeroes (i.e., it's a multiple of 100).\n* The year is a leap year only if it leaves a remainder of 200 or 600 when divided by 900.\n\nWe can start by listing the multiples of 100 between 1996 and 4096:\n\n100, 200, 300, ..., 4000\n\nNow, let's check which of these multiples of 100 leave a remainder of 200 or 600 when divided by 900:\n\n* 200: leaves a remainder of 200 when divided by 900 (OK)\n* 300: leaves a remainder of 300 when divided by 900 (not OK)\n* 400: leaves a remainder of 400 when divided by 900 (not OK)\n* 500: leaves a remainder of 500 when divided by 900 (not OK)\n* 600: leaves a remainder of 600 when divided by 900 (OK)\n* 700: leaves a remainder of 700 when divided by 900 (not OK)\n* 800: leaves a remainder of 800 when divided by 900 (not OK)\n* 900: leaves a remainder of 900 when divided by 900 (not OK)\n* 1000: leaves a remainder of 100 when divided by 900 (not OK)\n* 1100: leaves a remainder of 100 when divided by 900 (not OK)\n* ...\n* 4000: leaves a remainder of 0 when divided by 900 (not OK)\n\nWe found two multiples of 100 that leave a remainder of 200 or 600 when divided by 900:\n\n* 2000\n* 6000\n\nTherefore, there are only 2 leap years that end in double zeroes between 1996 and 4096 under this proposal.", token_ids=[10267, 596, 24564, 279, 14050, 1473, 9, 362, 1060, 10548, 304, 2033, 98543, 320, 72, 1770, 2637, 433, 596, 264, 5361, 315, 220, 1041, 4390, 9, 578, 1060, 374, 264, 32571, 1060, 1193, 422, 433, 11141, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 1049, 477, 220, 5067, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 382, 1687, 649, 1212, 555, 15182, 279, 66160, 315, 220, 1041, 1990, 220, 2550, 21, 323, 220, 12378, 21, 1473, 1041, 11, 220, 1049, 11, 220, 3101, 11, 61453, 220, 3443, 15, 271, 7184, 11, 1095, 596, 1817, 902, 315, 1521, 66160, 315, 220, 1041, 5387, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 1049, 477, 220, 5067, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 1473, 9, 220, 1049, 25, 11141, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 1049, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 320, 4012, 340, 9, 220, 3101, 25, 11141, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 3101, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 320, 1962, 10619, 340, 9, 220, 3443, 25, 11141, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 3443, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 320, 1962, 10619, 340, 9, 220, 2636, 25, 11141, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 2636, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 320, 1962, 10619, 340, 9, 220, 5067, 25, 11141, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 5067, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 320, 4012, 340, 9, 220, 7007, 25, 11141, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 7007, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 320, 1962, 10619, 340, 9, 220, 4728, 25, 11141, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 4728, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 320, 1962, 10619, 340, 9, 220, 7467, 25, 11141, 264, 27410, 315, 220, 7467, 994, 18255, 555, 220, 7467, 320, 1962, 10619, 340, 9, 220, 10