Output~2025-04-07 00:02:35.576047: [RequestOutput(request_id=607, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Come up with a creative way to use up a leftover can of soup. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 15936, 709, 449, 264, 11782, 1648, 311, 1005, 709, 264, 65543, 649, 315, 19724, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The eternal conundrum of the leftover can of soup! Here's a creative way to use it up:\n\n**Soup-er Soup Dumplings**\n\nTransform that leftover can of soup into a delicious and fun twist on traditional dumplings! Here's what you'll need:\n\n* 1 can of leftover soup (any type will do, but creamy soups like broccoli cheddar or tomato soup work particularly well)\n* 1 package of wonton wrappers (about 20-24 wrappers)\n* 1/4 cup of shredded cheddar cheese (optional)\n* 1/4 cup of chopped fresh herbs (such as parsley, chives, or scallions)\n* 1 egg, beaten (for egg wash)\n* Cooking oil or non-stick spray for frying\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. Preheat a large skillet or wok over medium-high heat.\n2. Open the can of soup and pour it into a bowl. Set aside.\n3. Lay a wonton wrapper on a flat surface. Place a tablespoon of the soup in the center of the wrapper.\n4. Sprinkle a pinch of shredded cheese and chopped herbs on top of the soup, if using.\n5. Dip your finger in the beaten egg and run it along the edges of the wrapper to create a seal.\n6. Fold the wrapper into a triangle by bringing the two opposite corners together to form a point. Press the edges together to seal the dumpling.\n7. Repeat with the remaining wrappers and soup.\n8. When the skillet or wok is hot, add a tablespoon of oil or non-stick spray. Fry the dumplings until they're golden brown on the bottom, about 2-3 minutes.\n9. Flip the dumplings and cook for an additional 2 minutes, until the other side is also golden brown.\n10. Serve the soup dumplings hot with your favorite dipping sauce. Enjoy!\n\nThis creative way to use up leftover soup is not only delicious, but it's also a fun and interactive meal that's perfect for a weeknight dinner or a weekend brunch. The wonton wrappers add a nice crunch and texture to the dish, while the soup provides a comforting and flavorful filling. Get creative with your soup choices and enjoy!", token_ids=[791, 35825, 390, 1263, 10952, 315, 279, 65543, 649, 315, 19724, 0, 5810, 596, 264, 11782, 1648, 311, 1005, 433, 709, 1473, 334, 33642, 12, 261, 61434, 65082, 81402, 57277, 9140, 430, 65543, 649, 315, 19724, 1139, 264, 18406, 323, 2523, 27744, 389, 8776, 63811, 81402, 0, 5810, 596, 1148, 499, 3358, 1205, 1473, 9, 220, 16, 649, 315, 65543, 19724, 320, 3852, 955, 690, 656, 11, 719, 47985, 5945, 1725, 1093, 79276, 523, 78716, 477, 42120, 19724, 990, 8104, 1664, 340, 9, 220, 16, 6462, 315, 40464, 263, 79194, 320, 9274, 220, 508, 12, 1187, 79194, 340, 9, 220, 16, 14, 19, 10747, 315, 75220, 523, 78716, 17604, 320, 13099, 340, 9, 220, 16, 14, 19, 10747, 315, 38525, 7878, 42393, 320, 21470, 439, 88621, 11, 523, 1924, 11, 477, 1156, 543, 919, 340, 9, 220, 16, 19151, 11, 31394, 320, 2000, 19151, 11623, 340, 9, 57410, 5707, 477, 2536, 5594, 875, 23749, 369, 87196, 271, 56391, 1473, 16, 13, 5075, 20559, 264, 3544, 79085, 477, 289, 564, 927, 11298, 28661, 8798, 627, 17, 13, 5377, 279, 649, 315, 19724, 323, 5019, 433, 1139, 264, 19763, 13, 2638, 16038, 627, 18, 13, 45024, 264, 40464, 263, 13564, 389, 264, 10269, 7479, 13, 11004, 264, 62611, 315, 279, 19724, 304, 279, 4219, 315, 279, 13564, 627, 19, 13, 15883, 36244, 264