Output~2025-04-07 00:03:36.667773: [RequestOutput(request_id=627, prompt='<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{"Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Generate a list of security best practices for a company\'s website. ### Response:"}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 5018, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 20400, 264, 1160, 315, 4868, 1888, 12659, 369, 264, 2883, 596, 3997, 13, 17010, 6075, 3047, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a list of security best practices for a company's website:\n\n**1. Keep Software Up-to-Date**\n\n* Regularly update your website's content management system (CMS), plugins, themes, and other software to ensure you have the latest security patches and features.\n* Use a reliable update mechanism to ensure timely updates.\n\n**2. Use Strong Passwords and Authentication**\n\n* Use strong, unique passwords for all user accounts, including administrator accounts.\n* Implement multi-factor authentication (MFA) to add an extra layer of security.\n* Limit login attempts and lock out users after a specified number of failed attempts.\n\n**3. Use HTTPS (SSL/TLS)**\n\n* Install an SSL/TLS certificate to encrypt data transmitted between your website and users' browsers.\n* Ensure all pages, including login pages, are served over HTTPS.\n\n**4. Validate and Sanitize User Input**\n\n* Validate all user input data, including forms, comments, and user-generated content.\n* Sanitize user input to prevent cross-site scripting (XSS) attacks.\n\n**5. Use a Web Application Firewall (WAF)**\n\n* Implement a WAF to detect and block common web attacks, such as SQL injection and cross-site request forgery (CSRF).\n* Configure the WAF to block suspicious traffic and monitor logs for potential threats.\n\n**6. Limit File Uploads and Storage**\n\n* Limit file uploads to specific directories and file types to prevent unauthorized file uploads.\n* Regularly review and purge unused files to prevent data breaches.\n\n**7. Monitor Website Logs and Activity**\n\n* Regularly review website logs to detect and respond to security incidents.\n* Monitor website activity, including login attempts, failed login attempts, and unusual traffic patterns.\n\n**8. Use a Secure Content Delivery Network (CDN)**\n\n* Use a CDN that provides SSL/TLS encryption and DDoS protection.\n* Configure the CDN to cache frequently accessed content and reduce the load on your website.\n\n**9. Implement a Secure Backup and Recovery Plan**\n\n* Regularly back up your website data, including database and files.\n* Test your backup and recovery plan to ensure it works in case of a disaster.\n\n**10. Conduct Regular Security Audits and Penetration Testing**\n\n* Conduct regular security audits to identify vulnerabilities and weaknesses.\n* Perform penetration testing to simulate attacks and identify potential entry points.\n\n**11. Use a Secure Email Service**\n\n* Use a secure email service that provides encryption and authentication.\n* Configure your email service to prevent spam and phishing attacks.\n\n**12. Limit Access to", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 1160, 315, 4868, 1888, 12659, 369, 264, 2883, 596, 3997, 1473, 334, 16, 13, 13969, 4476, 3216, 4791, 12, 1956, 57277, 9, 29900, 398, 2713, 701, 3997, 596, 2262, 6373, 1887, 320, 54357, 705, 17658, 11, 22100, 11, 323, 1023, 3241, 311, 6106, 499, 617, 279, 5652, 4868, 29760, 323, 4519, 627, 9, 5560, 264, 15062, 2713, 17383, 311, 6106, 32100, 9013, 382, 334, 17, 13, 5560, 27191, 12642, 82, 323, 24446, 57277, 9, 5560, 3831, 11, 5016, 34816, 369, 682, 1217, 9815, 11, 2737, 29193, 9815, 627, 9, 32175, 7447, 75197, 