Output~2025-04-07 00:04:42.565716: [RequestOutput(request_id=667, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the composition of Jupiter. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 18528, 315, 50789, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Jupiter is the largest planet in our solar system, with a composition that is primarily made up of hydrogen and helium gases. The planet's atmosphere is divided into three main layers: the troposphere, the stratosphere, and the thermosphere.\n\nThe troposphere is the lowest layer, extending from the planet's surface up to a height of about 50 km (31 miles). This layer is where the weather patterns on Jupiter occur, with strong winds and storm systems that can be thousands of kilometers wide. The troposphere is also where the planet's famous Great Red Spot, a persistent anticyclonic storm, is located.\n\nThe stratosphere is the next layer, extending from the troposphere up to a height of about 100 km (62 miles). This layer is characterized by a layer of sulfur and phosphorus compounds that absorb ultraviolet radiation from the sun, causing the stratosphere to glow.\n\nThe thermosphere is the outermost layer, extending from the stratosphere up to a height of about 10,000 km (6,200 miles). This layer is where the planet's magnetic field is located, and it is also where the aurorae, or northern and southern lights, occur.\n\nIn addition to these three main layers, Jupiter's composition also includes a dense core at its center, made up of iron and nickel. The core is surrounded by a thick layer of metallic hydrogen, which is thought to be responsible for the planet's strong magnetic field. The outer layers of the planet are made up of hydrogen and helium gases, which are the result of the planet's formation and evolution over billions of years.\n\nOverall, Jupiter's composition is a complex and dynamic system that is still being studied by scientists today. Its unique combination of gases, liquids, and solids makes it a fascinating and important object of study in the field of planetary science.", token_ids=[41, 20089, 374, 279, 7928, 11841, 304, 1057, 13238, 1887, 11, 449, 264, 18528, 430, 374, 15871, 1903, 709, 315, 35784, 323, 97607, 45612, 13, 578, 11841, 596, 16975, 374, 18255, 1139, 2380, 1925, 13931, 25, 279, 21965, 66222, 11, 279, 610, 14357, 8182, 11, 323, 279, 30945, 66222, 382, 791, 21965, 66222, 374, 279, 15821, 6324, 11, 33459, 505, 279, 11841, 596, 7479, 709, 311, 264, 2673, 315, 922, 220, 1135, 13437, 320, 2148, 8931, 570, 1115, 6324, 374, 1405, 279, 9282, 12912, 389, 50789, 12446, 11, 449, 3831, 29592, 323, 13766, 6067, 430, 649, 387, 9214, 315, 41668, 7029, 13, 578, 21965, 66222, 374, 1101, 1405, 279, 11841, 596, 11495, 8681, 3816, 24178, 11, 264, 26048, 3276, 2912, 566, 14338, 13766, 11, 374, 7559, 382, 791, 610, 14357, 8182, 374, 279, 1828, 6324, 11, 33459, 505, 279, 21965, 66222, 709, 311, 264, 2673, 315, 922, 220, 1041, 13437, 320, 5538, 8931, 570, 1115, 6324, 374, 32971, 555, 264, 6324, 315, 72591, 323, 33088, 30969, 32246, 430, 35406, 37232, 85311, 25407, 505, 279, 7160, 11, 14718, 279, 610, 14357, 8182, 311, 37066, 382, 791, 30945, 66222, 374, 279, 16335, 3646, 6324, 11, 33459, 505, 279, 610, 14357, 8182, 709, 311, 264, 2673, 315, 922, 220, 605, 11, 931, 13437, 320, 21, 11, 1049, 8931, 570, 1115, 6324, 374, 1405, 279, 11841, 596, 24924, 2115, 374, 7559, 11, 323, 433, 374, 1101, 1405, 279, 44521, 269, 6043, 11, 477, 18671, 323, 18561, 13001, 11, 12446, 3