Output~2025-04-07 00:06:54.494709: [RequestOutput(request_id=710, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a memo to inform employees about the new dress code policy. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 22154, 311, 6179, 8420, 922, 279, 502, 8679, 2082, 4947, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="**MEMORANDUM**\n\n**Subject: New Dress Code Policy**\n\n**To: All Employees**\n\n**Date:** [Current Date]\n\nAs we continue to strive for excellence in our industry, we are introducing a new dress code policy to enhance our professional image and promote a positive work environment. This policy is designed to ensure that all employees present themselves in a manner that reflects our company's values and standards.\n\n**Purpose:**\n\nThe purpose of this policy is to establish a clear and consistent dress code that applies to all employees, regardless of their role or department. This policy aims to promote a professional and respectful atmosphere, while also allowing for individual expression and comfort.\n\n**Policy:**\n\nThe new dress code policy is as follows:\n\n* Business casual attire is expected for all employees, with the following guidelines:\n\t+ Tops: Blouses, polo shirts, or button-down shirts are acceptable. Avoid low-cut or revealing tops.\n\t+ Bottoms: Slacks, khakis, or skirts/dresses that are knee-length or longer are acceptable. Avoid ripped or distressed denim.\n\t+ Footwear: Closed-toe shoes with a low to moderate heel are recommended. Sandals, flip-flops, and open-toed shoes are not permitted.\n\t+ Accessories: Simple jewelry, watches, and belts are acceptable. Avoid excessive or flashy jewelry.\n* Special occasions: For special events, meetings, or presentations, employees are expected to dress in business attire, which includes a suit and tie for men, and a blouse or dress for women.\n\n**Exceptions:**\n\n* Employees who work in specific roles that require a more relaxed dress code, such as customer-facing positions, will be notified by their supervisor.\n* Employees who have a medical condition or religious belief that requires a specific dress code accommodation should notify their supervisor in advance to discuss reasonable accommodations.\n\n**Enforcement:**\n\nThe dress code policy will be enforced by management and supervisors. Employees who fail to comply with the policy may be subject to verbal warnings, written warnings, or disciplinary action, up to and including termination.\n\n**Effective Date:**\n\nThis policy will take effect on [Date] and will be reviewed annually or as needed.\n\n**Questions and Feedback:**\n\nIf you have any questions or concerns about the new dress code policy, please reach out to your supervisor or HR representative. We value your feedback and appreciate your cooperation in implementing this new policy.\n\nThank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\nSincerely,\n\n[Your Name]\n[Your Title]", token_ids=[334, 33070, 878, 4064, 2864, 57277, 334, 13317, 25, 1561, 29318, 6247, 11216, 57277, 334, 1271, 25, 2052, 44741, 57277, 334, 1956, 68063, 510, 5520, 2696, 2595, 2170, 584, 3136, 311, 37106, 369, 38656, 304, 1057, 5064, 11, 584, 527, 33018, 264, 502, 8679, 2082, 4947, 311, 18885, 1057, 6721, 2217, 323, 12192, 264, 6928, 990, 4676, 13, 1115, 4947, 374, 6319, 311, 6106, 430, 682, 8420, 3118, 5694, 304, 264, 11827, 430, 27053, 1057, 2883, 596, 2819, 323, 10886, 382, 334, 75133, 25, 57277, 791, 7580, 315, 420, 4947, 374, 311, 5813, 264, 2867, 323, 1