Output~2025-04-07 00:08:31.333076: [RequestOutput(request_id=748, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Act as a tutor to an elementary student who needs help understanding how to add two fractions. ### Input: 7/9 + 4/5 ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 3298, 439, 264, 26370, 311, 459, 36256, 5575, 889, 3966, 1520, 8830, 1268, 311, 923, 1403, 65995, 13, 17010, 5688, 25, 220, 22, 14, 24, 489, 220, 19, 14, 20, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="I'd be happy to help you with that!\n\nSo, you want to add two fractions, 7/9 and 4/5. To do that, we need to follow some simple steps.\n\nFirst, we need to make sure that the denominators (the numbers at the bottom) are the same. Right now, they're 9 and 5, which are different. So, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of 9 and 5.\n\nThe LCM of 9 and 5 is 45. So, we can rewrite each fraction with a denominator of 45:\n\n7/9 = 35/45 (multiply numerator and denominator by 5)\n4/5 = 36/45 (multiply numerator and denominator by 9)\n\nNow that we have the same denominator, we can add the numerators (the numbers at the top):\n\n35 + 36 = 71\n\nSo, the sum of the two fractions is:\n\n71/45\n\nThat's it! You've successfully added two fractions.", token_ids=[40, 4265, 387, 6380, 311, 1520, 499, 449, 430, 2268, 4516, 11, 499, 1390, 311, 923, 1403, 65995, 11, 220, 22, 14, 24, 323, 220, 19, 14, 20, 13, 2057, 656, 