Output~2025-04-07 00:13:49.807297: [RequestOutput(request_id=869, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: What were the main elements of the Hundred Days Reform of 1898? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 3639, 1051, 279, 1925, 5540, 315, 279, 88370, 21882, 40365, 315, 220, 9378, 23, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The Hundred Days Reform of 1898, also known as the Guangxu Emperor's Reform Movement, was a series of reforms implemented in China from June 11 to September 21, 1898, during the late Qing dynasty. The main elements of the reform movement were:\n\n1. **Establishment of a new cabinet system**: The Qing government established a new cabinet system, with a prime minister and a council of ministers, to centralize power and streamline decision-making.\n2. **Promotion of education and modernization**: The reformers emphasized the importance of education and modernization, introducing new schools, universities, and vocational training programs to promote scientific and technological advancements.\n3. **Reorganization of the military**: The Qing government reorganized the military, introducing a new conscription system, modernizing the army's equipment and training, and establishing a naval academy.\n4. **Economic reforms**: The reformers aimed to modernize China's economy by promoting foreign investment, establishing a new banking system, and introducing a gold standard.\n5. **Constitutional reforms**: The Qing government drafted a new constitution, which would have established a constitutional monarchy and limited the power of the emperor.\n6. **Expansion of local self-government**: The reformers aimed to decentralize power by establishing a system of local self-government, giving more autonomy to provinces and counties.\n7. **Promotion of women's rights**: The reformers introduced measures to promote women's rights, including the establishment of women's schools and the abolition of foot binding.\n\nThese reforms were ambitious and far-reaching, but they were ultimately unsuccessful due to opposition from conservative elements within the Qing government and the Chinese society. The reform movement was halted after only 104 days, and the Qing government returned to its traditional policies.", token_ids=[791, 88370, 21882, 40365, 315, 220, 9378, 23, 11, 1101, 3967, 439, 279, 65537, 87, 84, 35414, 596, 40365, 29098, 11, 574, 264, 4101, 315, 31343, 11798, 304, 5734, 505, 5651, 220, 806, 311, 6250, 220, 1691, 11, 220, 9378, 23, 11, 2391, 279, 3389, 63012, 67946, 13, 578, 1925, 5540, 315, 279, 15180, 7351, 1051, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 69320, 479, 315, 264, 502, 22685, 1887, 96618, 578, 63012, 3109, 9749, 264, 502, 22685, 1887, 11, 449, 264, 10461, 13015, 323, 264, 15177, 315, 35050, 11, 311, 8792, 553, 2410, 323, 82703, 5597, 28846, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 36286, 6082, 315, 6873, 323, 6617, 2065, 96618, 578, 15180, 388, 46728, 279, 12939, 315, 6873, 323, 6617, 2065, 11, 33018, 502, 8853, 11, 23978, 11, 323, 89486, 4967, 7620, 311, 12192, 12624, 323, 30116, 83787, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 697, 24844, 315, 279, 6411, 96618, 578, 63012, 3109, 312, 63316, 279, 6411, 11, 33018, 264, 502, 1615, 1479, 1887, 11, 6617, 4954, 279, 13695, 596, 7241, 323, 4967, 11, 323, 31692, 264, 46398, 44445, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 36, 32107, 31343, 96618, 578, 15180, 388, 20034, 311, 6617, 553, 5734, 596, 8752, 555, 22923, 7362, 9341, 11, 31692, 264, 502, 23641, 1887, 11, 323, 33018, 264, 6761, 5410, 627, 20, 13, 3146, 1128, 10663, 278, 31343, 96618, 5