Output~2025-04-07 00:14:11.284779: [RequestOutput(request_id=873, prompt='<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{\'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a story that begins with "It was a cold, dark night". ### Response:\'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 3446, 430, 12302, 449, 330, 2181, 574, 264, 9439, 11, 6453, 3814, 3343, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='It was a cold, dark night, the kind that made you want to curl up by the fire with a good book and a warm cup of tea. But I wasn\'t going to get that luxury. I had a job to do, and it couldn\'t wait until morning.\n\nI bundled up in my coat and boots, grabbed my flashlight, and set out into the darkness. The streets were empty, save for the occasional passing car, its headlights casting an eerie glow over the deserted sidewalks. I walked quickly, my eyes scanning the pavement for any sign of what I was looking for.\n\nAs I turned the corner onto Main Street, I saw it: a small, unassuming building with a sign that read "The Old Bookshop". I had been searching for this place for weeks, and finally, I had found it. I pushed open the creaky door and stepped inside.\n\nThe shop was dimly lit, the air thick with the scent of old books and dust. Shelves upon shelves of volumes stretched up to the ceiling, their leather-bound covers creaking softly as I moved through the aisles. I ran my fingers over the spines, feeling the raised letters and intricate designs.\n\nAt the back of the shop, I found what I was looking for: a small, leather-bound book with a strange symbol etched into the cover. I opened it, and a musty smell wafted out. The pages were yellowed and crackling, but as I turned them, I saw that they were filled with handwritten notes and diagrams.\n\nI spent hours poring over the book, my eyes scanning the pages for any clues that might lead me to what I was searching for. As the night wore on, the cold and darkness outside seemed to fade away, replaced by a sense of excitement and discovery. I knew that I had stumbled upon something big, something that could change everything.\n\nAs the first light of dawn began to creep into the sky, I closed the book and tucked it into my bag. I had a long journey ahead of me, but I was ready. I had found what I was looking for, and nothing was going to stop me from uncovering its secrets.', token_ids=[2181, 574, 264, 9439, 11, 6453, 3814, 11, 279, 3169, 430, 1903, 499, 1390, 311, 14284, 709, 555, 279, 4027, 449, 264, 1695, 2363, 323, 264, 8369, 10747, 315, 15600, 13, 2030, 358, 5828, 956, 2133, 311, 636, 430, 19913, 13, 358, 1047, 264, 2683, 311, 656, 11, 323, 433, 7846, 956, 3868, 3156, 6693, 382, 40, 52550, 709, 304, 856, 23724, 323, 26302, 11, 30418, 856, 79515, 11, 323, 743, 704, 1139, 279, 27394, 13, 578, 14708, 1051, 4384, 11, 3665, 369, 279, 28961, 12579, 1841, 11, 1202, 88720, 25146, 459, 97383, 37066, 927, 279, 83410, 82835, 13, 358, 15203, 6288, 11, 856, 6548, 36201, 279, 65442, 369, 904, 1879, 315, 1148, 358, 574, 3411, 369, 382, 2170, 358, 6656, 279, 9309, 8800, 4802, 6825, 11, 358, 5602, 433, 25, 264, 2678, 11, 653, 66463, 4857, 449, 264, 1879, 430, 1373, 330, 791, 10846, 6017, 8845, 3343, 358, 1047, 1027, 15389, 369, 420, 2035, 369, 5672, 11, 323, 5616, 11, 358, 1047, 1766, 433, 13, 358, 15753, 1825, 279, 272, 1127, 88, 6134, 323, 25319, 4871, 382, 791, 8221, 574, 5213, 398, 13318, 11, 279, 3805, 12314, 449, 279, 41466, 315, 2362, 6603, 323, 16174, 13, 1443, 4372, 5304, 36310, 315, 27378, 41398, 709, 311, 279, 22959, 11, 872, 18012, 50962, 14861, 