 and administrative tasks"\n\t+ Example: "Digital payments automate many administrative tasks, freeing up time for more important tasks"\n\n**IV. Security**\n\n* Subpoint 1: "Enhanced security features"\n\t+ Example: "Digital payments use advanced encryption and secure servers to protect sensitive information"\n* Subpoint 2: "Reduced risk of fraud"\n\t+ Example: "Digital payments are less susceptible to fraud, as transactions are recorded and monitored in real-time"\n\n**V. Cost Savings**\n\n* Subpoint 1: "Reduced transaction fees"\n\t+ Example: "Digital payments often have lower transaction fees compared to traditional payment methods"\n* Subpoint 2: "Increased transparency"\n\t+ Example: "Digital payments provide clear and transparent records of transactions, making it easier to track expenses and manage finances"\n\n**VI. Conclusion**\n\n* Restate thesis statement\n* Summarize key points\n* Final thought: "In conclusion, digital payments offer numerous benefits that make them a more convenient, efficient, and secure way to conduct transactions. As technology continues to evolve, it\'s clear that digital payments will play an increasingly important role in our daily lives."\n\nThis outline provides a general structure for a speech on the benefits of using digital payments. You can expand on each point and add more examples to make the speech more engaging and informative.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 4754, 8982, 21782, 389, 279, 8712, 330, 85423, 315, 1701, 7528, 14507, 304, 3432, 596, 1917, 52518, 334, 40, 13, 29438, 57277, 9, 29271, 25, 330, 644, 3432, 596, 5043, 65319, 1917, 11, 279, 1648, 584, 1304, 14507, 374, 10223, 19019, 702, 9, 75097, 5224, 25, 330, 39212, 14507, 3085, 12387, 7720, 430, 1304, 1124, 264, 810, 17125, 11, 11297, 11, 323, 9966, 1648, 311, 6929, 14463, 1875, 334, 5660, 13, 81748, 57277, 9, 3804, 2837, 220, 16, 25, 330, 1187, 14, 22, 40800, 702, 197, 10, 13688, 25, 330, 2409, 7528, 14507, 11, 499, 649, 1304, 14463, 520, 904, 892, 323, 505, 904,