* Subject line: The subject line of the email can also be a good indicator of whether the email is spam or not.\n\t* Reply-to address: The reply-to address can also be a good indicator of whether the email is spam or not.\n3. **Metadata Features**:\n\t* Date and time: The date and time the email was sent can be a good indicator of whether the email is spam or not.\n\t* IP address: The IP address of the sender can be a good indicator of whether the email is spam or not.\n\n**Model Selection**\n\nOnce we have extracted the features, we need to select a suitable machine learning model to classify the emails. Some possible models that can be used include:\n\n1. **Naive Bayes**: A simple and effective model that can be used for text classification.\n2. **Logistic Regression**: A linear model that can be used for binary classification.\n3. **Decision Trees**: A tree-based model that can be used for classification.\n4. **Random Forest**: An ensemble model that combines multiple decision trees to improve the accuracy of the model.\n\n**Model Training**\n\nOnce we have selected the model, we need to train it using the dataset. We can split the dataset into training and testing sets, and then train the model on the training set and evaluate its performance on the', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2077, 430, 45695, 279, 1715, 1473, 334, 86140, 5008, 369, 82767, 6296, 13, 11842, 6354, 79, 309, 72966, 57277, 334, 34463, 11348, 57277, 1271, 1977, 264, 24790, 1646, 11, 584, 1205, 264, 10550, 315, 30929, 14633, 13, 1226, 649, 6667, 264, 10550, 315, 14633, 430, 527, 30929, 439, 3060, 330, 76645, 1, 477, 330, 6414, 23032, 309, 3343, 1226, 649, 1005, 17880, 2561, 30525, 1778, 439, 279, 2998, 2298, 8463, 40283, 477, 279, 82767, 5733, 44823, 3142, 76834, 382, 334, 14180, 95606, 57277, 12805, 584, 617, 279, 10550, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 8819, 9959, 4519, 505, 1855, 2613, 430, 649, 1520, 279, 1646, 49229, 433, 439, 26396, 477, 2536, 23032, 309, 13, 4427, 3284, 4519, 430, 649, 387, 28532, 2997, 14