 generations, and temperature (which controls the randomness of the generated text).\n3. **Generate text**: Use the `generate` method of the GPT-2 model to generate text based on the input prompt. You can specify the number of generations (i.e., the number of sentences or paragraphs) you want the model to generate.\n4. **Post-processing**: You can further process the generated text by removing unnecessary tokens, formatting the text, or applying additional filters.\n\n**Example Code:**\n```python\nimport torch\nfrom transformers import GPT2ForSequenceClassification, GPT2Tokenizer\n\n# Load the GPT-2 model and tokenizer\nmodel = GPT2ForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(\'gpt2\')\ntokenizer = GPT2Tokenizer.from_pretrained(\'gpt2\')\n\n# Prepare the input prompt\nprompt = "Write a short story about a futuristic city."\n\n# Set the model\'s parameters\nmax_length = 100\nnum_generations = 3\ntemperature = 0.7\n\n# Generate text\ninput_ids = tokenizer.encode(prompt, return_tensors=\'pt\')\noutput = model.generate(input_ids, max_length=max', token_ids=[334, 16834, 264, 480, 2898, 12, 17, 5008, 311, 20400, 2991, 57277, 38, 2898, 12, 17, 320, 5648, 1413, 5075, 70024, 63479, 220, 17, 8, 374, 264, 955, 315, 4221, 1646, 8040, 555, 5377, 15836, 430, 649, 7068, 3823, 12970, 1495, 3196, 389, 264, 2728, 10137, 477, 1988, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 3094, 14656, 30308, 8641, 389, 1268, 311, 1005, 264, 480, 2898, 12, 17, 1646, 311, 7068, 1495, 1473, 334, 3617, 83401, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 3146, 25017, 264, 480, 2898, 12, 17, 1646, 96618, 8593, 264, 864, 70024, 480, 2898, 12, 17, 1646, 430, 29076, 701, 3966, 13, 1472, 649, 1005, 279, 4113, 480, 2898, 12, 17, 1646, 477, 832, 315, 1202, 27103, 11, 1778, 439, 480, 2898, 12, 17, 15344, 11, 25352, 11, 477, 20902, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 25718, 279, 5995, 20797, 96618, 19796, 279, 473, 36368, 19109, 81632, 6875, 11, 902, 5825, 459, 3834, 311, 279, 480, 2898, 12, 17, 1646, 13, 1472, 649, 4685, 433, 1701, 24547, 25, 1595, 52601, 4685, 87970, 19154, 18, 