Output~2025-04-07 00:21:54.470182: [RequestOutput(request_id=1036, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: What items could a person put in an emergency kit? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 3639, 3673, 1436, 264, 1732, 2231, 304, 459, 13147, 16530, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="An emergency kit, also known as a 72-hour kit or disaster supply kit, is a collection of essential items that can help a person or family survive for at least three days in case of an emergency or natural disaster. Here are some items that a person could put in an emergency kit:\n\n**Water and Food:**\n\n* At least three days' worth of bottled water (one gallon per person per day)\n* Non-perishable, high-calorie food such as energy bars, canned goods, and MREs\n* Manual can opener\n* Cooking equipment, such as a portable stove or camping stove\n* Fuel for cooking, such as propane or charcoal\n\n**First Aid and Hygiene:**\n\n* First aid kit with bandages, antiseptic wipes, pain relievers, and any prescription medications\n* Moist towelettes, garbage bags, and plastic ties for personal hygiene\n* Feminine hygiene products, if applicable\n* Moisturizer and sunscreen\n\n**Shelter and Warmth:**\n\n* Tent or tarpaulin\n* Sleeping bag or blanket\n* Extra clothing, including warm layers and rain gear\n* Flashlight or headlamp\n* Extra batteries\n* Fire starting equipment, such as matches, lighters, or a fire starter\n\n**Communication and Tools:**\n\n* Cell phone with charger and back-up battery\n* Two-way radio or walkie-talkie\n* Whistle to signal for help\n* Multi-tool or pocket knife\n* Duct tape\n* Local maps\n\n**Personal Documents:**\n\n* Copies of important documents, such as identification, insurance cards, and birth certificates\n* Cash and credit cards\n* Small notebook and pen\n\n**Other:**\n\n* Pet supplies, such as food, water, and medication\n* Child and infant supplies, such as diapers, formula, and baby wipes\n* Important medications, such as epinephrine auto-injectors or inhalers\n* Sanitation supplies, such as toilet paper and hand sanitizer\n\nRemember to check your emergency kit regularly to ensure that all items are still usable and not expired. It's also a good idea to customize your kit to fit your specific needs and the types of emergencies that are most likely to occur in your area.", token_ids=[2127, 13147, 16530, 11, 1101, 3967, 439, 264, 220, 5332, 21925, 16530, 477, 21426, 8312, 16530, 11, 374, 264, 4526, 315, 7718, 3673, 430, 649, 1520, 264, 1732, 477, 3070, 18167, 369, 520, 3325, 2380, 2919, 304, 1162, 315, 459, 13147, 477, 5933, 21426, 13, 5810, 527, 1063, 3673, 430, 264, 1732, 1436, 2231, 304, 459, 13147, 16530, 1473, 334, 29353, 323, 12369, 25, 57277, 9, 2468, 3325, 2380, 2919, 6, 5922, 315, 72178, 3090, 320, 606, 50680, 824, 1732, 824, 1938, 340, 9, 11842, 17453, 819, 481, 11, 1579, 49236, 30303, 3691, 1778, 439, 4907, 16283, 11, 64114, 11822, 11, 323, 386, 793, 82, 198, 9, 14881, 649, 36253, 198, 9, 57410, 7241, 11, 1778, 439, 264, 23665, 45115, 477, 33873, 45115, 198, 9, 37384, 369, 17677, 11, 1778, 439, 92038, 477, 61203, 271, 334, 5451, 38505, 323, 10320, 43312, 25, 57277, 9, 5629, 12576, 16530, 449, 7200, 1154, 11, 3276, 1082, 27330, 84638, 11, 6784, 59644, 3078, 11, 323, 904, 22866, 31010, 198, 9, 82804, 311, 906, 66692, 11, 26964, 18381, 11, 323, 12466, 20405, 369, 4443, 53056, 198, 9, 57401, 483, 53056, 3956, 11, 422, 8581, 198, 9, 82804, 324, 3213, 323, 83184, 271, 334, 2059, 18354, 323, 46863