Output~2025-04-07 00:25:35.236847: [RequestOutput(request_id=1132, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the events that happen during mitosis. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 4455, 430, 3621, 2391, 5568, 10934, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Mitosis is the process of cell division that results in two daughter cells that are genetically identical to the parent cell. The events that occur during mitosis can be divided into several stages:\n\n**Interphase**: This is the longest stage of the cell cycle, during which the cell grows, replicates its DNA, and prepares for cell division. The chromatin, which is the DNA and proteins that make up the chromosomes, condenses into visible chromosomes.\n\n**Prophase**: In this stage, the chromatin condenses further into visible chromosomes, and the nuclear envelope breaks down. The centrioles, which are small structures near the nucleus, begin to move apart and form a spindle apparatus. The spindle fibers, which are made up of microtubules, attach to the centromeres of the chromosomes.\n\n**Prometaphase**: The nuclear envelope breaks down completely, and the chromosomes are released into the cytoplasm. The spindle fibers continue to grow and attach to the chromosomes.\n\n**Metaphase**: The chromosomes line up at the center of the cell, attached to the spindle fibers. This is known as the metaphase plate.\n\n**Anaphase**: The sister chromatids, which are identical copies of each chromosome, separate and move to opposite poles of the cell. The spindle fibers contract, causing the sister chromatids to move apart.\n\n**Telophase**: The chromosomes reach the poles of the cell and begin to uncoil, returning to their interphase structure. The nuclear envelope reforms around each set of chromosomes.\n\n**Cytokinesis**: In this final stage, the cytoplasm divides and the cell splits into two daughter cells. In animal cells, this is achieved through the formation of a cleavage furrow, while in plant cells, it occurs through the formation of a cell plate.\n\nOverall, mitosis is a complex process that ensures the accurate transmission of genetic information from one generation of cells to the next.', token_ids=[55470, 10934, 374, 279, 1920, 315, 2849, 13096, 430, 3135, 304, 1403, 10003, 7917, 430, 527, 52033, 20086, 311, 279, 2748, 2849, 13, 578, 4455, 430, 12446, 2391, 5568, 10934, 649, 387, 18255, 1139, 3892, 18094, 1473, 334, 3386, 26199, 96618, 1115, 374, 279, 22807, 6566, 315, 279, 2849, 11008, 11, 2391, 902, 279, 2849, 28815, 11, 29641, 988, 1202, 15922, 11, 323, 48542, 369, 2849, 13096, 13, 578, 22083, 15111, 11, 902, 374, 279, 15922, 323, 28896, 430, 1304, 709, 279, 83181, 11, 9955, 4377, 1139, 9621, 83181, 382, 334, 1360, 26199, 96618, 763, 420, 6566, 11, 279, 22083, 15111, 9955, 4377, 4726, 1139, 9621, 83181, 11, 323, 279, 11499, 35498, 18808, 1523, 13, 578, 2960, 462, 7298, 11, 902, 527, 2678, 14726, 3221, 279, 62607, 11, 3240, 311, 3351, 10980, 323, 1376, 264, 99291, 41705, 13, 578, 99291, 49774, 11, 902, 527, 1903, 709, 315, 8162, 83, 392, 2482, 11, 15866, 311, 279, 2960, 442, 13213, 315, 279, 83181, 382, 334, 36286, 295, 1366, 521, 96618, 578, 11499, 35498, 18808, 1523, 6724, 11, 323, 279, 83181, 527, 6004, 1139, 279, 9693, 99705, 10753, 13, 578, 99291, 49774, 3136, 311, 3139, 323, 15866, 311, 279, 83181, 382, 334, 35773, 1366, 521, 96618, 578, 83181, 1584, 709, 520, 279, 4219, 315, 279, 2849, 11, 12673, 311, 279, 99291, 49774, 13, 1115, 374, 3