Output~2025-04-07 00:32:16.919642: [RequestOutput(request_id=1270, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe a scary situation ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 264, 29565, 6671, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='As I walked through the abandoned asylum, the creaking of the old wooden floorboards beneath my feet echoed through the deserted halls. The air was thick with the stench of decay and rot, and the flickering fluorescent lights above cast eerie shadows on the walls. I had always been drawn to the supernatural and the unknown, and this place was rumored to be one of the most haunted locations in the country.\n\nAs I explored the decaying building, I stumbled upon a room that seemed frozen in time. The hospital beds were still made, the wheelchairs were still parked in the corners, and the medical equipment was still scattered about. But it was the patient files that caught my attention. They were stacked high on a shelf, bound in worn leather and adorned with rusty metal clasps.\n\nAs I began to flip through the files, I noticed that they all had one thing in common: they were all from patients who had been admitted to the asylum decades ago, and they had all been diagnosed with the same condition: "acute schizophrenia." But as I delved deeper into the files, I began to notice something strange. The patients\' symptoms were all eerily similar, and the treatments they had received were all equally bizarre.\n\nSuddenly, I heard a faint whispering in my ear. It was soft and raspy, and it seemed to be coming from all around me. The words were indistinguishable, but the tone was unmistakable - it was a voice, and it was trying to communicate with me. I spun around, but there was no one there. The whispering grew louder, more urgent, and I felt a chill run down my spine.\n\nI tried to shake off the feeling of unease, but it was too late. The lights began to flicker, and the shadows on the walls seemed to move of their own accord. I knew then that I was not alone in the asylum, and that I was being watched. The voice in my ear grew louder, more insistent, and I knew that I had to get out of there - fast.\n\nI turned and ran, my heart pounding in my chest. I didn\'t stop until I was back in the bright sunlight, gasping for air. As I looked back at the asylum, I could have sworn I saw a figure standing in the window, watching me. I knew then that I would never set foot in that place again, and that I would never forget the terror I felt in that abandoned asylum.', token_ids=[2170, 358, 15203, 1555, 279, 23838, 33270, 11, 279, 272, 1127, 287, 315, 279, 2362, 23162, 6558, 19826, 24923, 856, 7693, 55212, 1555, 279, 83410, 52473, 13, 578, 3805, 574, 12314, 449, 279, 357, 20345, 315, 31815, 323, 5868, 11, 323, 279, 29447, 4776, 74864, 13001, 3485, 6445, 97383, 35612, 389, 279, 14620, 13, 358, 1047, 2744, 1027, 15107, 311, 279, 50058, 323, 279, 9987, 11, 323, 420, 2035, 574, 70468, 311, 387, 832, 315, 279, 1455, 57775, 10687, 304, 279, 3224, 382, 2170, 358, 36131, 279, 1654, 17718, 4857, 11, 358, 50157, 5304, 264, 3130, 430, 9508, 20268, 304, 892, 13, 578, 8952, 28036, 1051, 2103, 1903, 11, 279, 13587, 331, 4825, 1051, 2103, 43335, 304, 279, 24359, 11, 323, 279, 6593, 7241, 574, 2103, 38067, 922, 13, 2030, 433, 574, 279, 8893, 3626, 430, 10791, 856, 6666, 13, 2435, 1051, 42415, 1579, 389, 264, 28745, 11, 6965, 304, 24634, 18012, 323, 84273, 449, 98553, 9501, 57220, 1725, 382, 2170, 358, 6137, 311, 18791, 155