Output~2025-04-07 00:33:04.819888: [RequestOutput(request_id=1283, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Create a list of five books that everyone should read. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4324, 264, 1160, 315, 4330, 6603, 430, 5127, 1288, 1373, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='What a great task! Here are five books that I believe everyone should read, in no particular order:\n\n1. **"To Kill a Mockingbird" by Harper Lee**: This Pulitzer Prize-winning novel is a timeless classic that explores issues of racial injustice, tolerance, and the loss of innocence in a small Alabama town during the 1930s. Through the eyes of a young girl named Scout Finch, Lee masterfully weaves a story that is both poignant and thought-provoking.\n2. **"The Alchemist" by Paulo Coelho**: This fable-like novel follows a young shepherd named Santiago on a journey to fulfill his dreams and find his Personal Legend. The book is a beautiful exploration of spirituality, self-discovery, and the power of listening to one\'s heart.\n3. **"1984" by George Orwell**: This dystopian novel is a chilling warning about the dangers of totalitarianism and the erosion of individual freedom. Set in a future where the government exercises total control over its citizens, "1984" is a must-read for anyone interested in understanding the importance of critical thinking and the value of individual liberty.\n4. **"The Diary of a Young Girl" by Anne Frank**: This powerful and poignant memoir is a testament to the human spirit and the importance of hope and resilience in the face of adversity. Written by a young girl who was forced to hide with her family during the Nazi occupation of the Netherlands, the diary is a heart-wrenching account of the human experience during World War II.\n5. **"Sapiens: A Brief History of Humankind" by Yuval Noah Harari**: This sweeping narrative covers the entire history of humankind, from the emergence of Homo sapiens in Africa to the present day. Harari\'s book is a thought-provoking exploration of our species\' greatest achievements and failures, and offers a unique perspective on our place in the world.\n\nThese five books offer a diverse range of perspectives, styles, and themes, but all share a common thread of exploring the human condition. They are books that can inspire, educate, and challenge readers, and are essential reading for anyone looking to broaden their understanding of the world and their place in it.', token_ids=[3923, 264, 2294, 3465, 0, 5810, 527, 4330, 6603, 430, 358, 4510, 5127, 1288, 1373, 11, 304, 912, 4040, 2015, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 1, 1271, 27933, 264, 14905, 287, 23414, 1, 555, 33107, 12336, 96618, 1115, 96815, 32293, 27875, 11775, 374, 264, 58105, 11670, 430, 41424, 4819, 315, 19739, 51215, 11, 25065, 11, 323, 279, 4814, 315, 57311, 304, 264, 2678, 21272, 6424, 2391, 279, 220, 7285, 15, 82, 13, 17331, 279, 6548, 315, 264, 3995, 3828, 7086, 48635, 96333, 11, 12336, 7491, 3725, 584, 4798, 264, 3446, 430, 374, 2225, 93447, 323, 3463, 10039, 85, 10979, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 1, 791, 1708, 75188, 1, 555, 38026, 3623, 87099, 96618, 1115, 282, 481, 12970, 11775, 11263, 264, 3995, 91478, 7086, 55678, 389, 264, 11879, 311, 21054, 813, 19226, 323, 1505, 813, 19758, 28033, 13, 578, 2363, 374, 264, 6366, 27501, 315, 75456, 11, 659, 10694, 7601, 11, 323, 279, 2410, 315, 14624, 311, 832, 596, 4851, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 1, 3753, 19, 1, 555, 10058, 83853, 96618, 1115, 69110, 48748, 11775, 374, 264, 62724, 10163, 9