Output~2025-04-07 00:33:32.229635: [RequestOutput(request_id=1299, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Name three differences between mammals and reptiles. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4076, 2380, 12062, 1990, 56669, 323, 64873, 3742, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are three differences between mammals and reptiles:\n\n1. **Body Temperature Regulation**: Mammals are endothermic, meaning they regulate their own body temperature, whereas reptiles are ectothermic, meaning they rely on external sources of heat to regulate their body temperature.\n2. **Skin and Scales**: Mammals have hair or fur, while reptiles have scales. Mammals also have sweat glands, which help to regulate their body temperature, whereas reptiles do not.\n3. **Reproduction**: Mammals give birth to live young and produce milk to feed their offspring, whereas reptiles lay eggs and do not produce milk to feed their young.', token_ids=[8586, 527, 2380, 12062, 1990, 56669, 323, 64873, 3742, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 5561, 38122, 48338, 96618, 386, 8836, 1147, 527, 842, 1605, 21914, 11, 7438, 814, 37377, 872, 1866, 2547, 9499, 11, 20444, 64873, 3742, 527, 77594, 1605, 21914, 11, 7438, 814, 17631, 389, 9434, 8336, 315, 8798, 311, 37377, 872, 2547, 9499, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 38286, 323, 328, 31296, 96618, 386, 8836, 1147, 617, 7013, 477, 18742, 11, 1418, 64873, 3742, 617, 29505, 13, 386, 8836, 1147, 1101, 617, 28566, 82375, 11, 902, 1520, 311, 37377, 872, 2547, 9499, 11, 20444, 64