Output~2025-04-07 00:37:13.194570: [RequestOutput(request_id=1362, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: What is the x-intercept of the line perpendicular to the line defined by 3x-2y = 6 and whose y-intercept is 2? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 3639, 374, 279, 865, 45994, 1512, 315, 279, 1584, 77933, 311, 279, 1584, 4613, 555, 220, 18, 87, 12, 17, 88, 284, 220, 21, 323, 6832, 379, 45994, 1512, 374, 220, 17, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='To find the x-intercept of the line perpendicular to the line 3x - 2y = 6 and whose y-intercept is 2, we need to first find the slope of the given line.\n\nThe given line is in the form Ax + By = C, where A = 3, B = -2, and C = 6. To find the slope, we can rewrite the equation in the slope-intercept form (y = mx + b), where m is the slope.\n\nRearranging the equation, we get:\n\n2y = 3x - 6\ny = (3/2)x - 3\n\nThe slope of the line is m = 3/2.\n\nThe line perpendicular to this line has a slope that is the negative reciprocal of 3/2, which is -2/3.\n\nThe line with y-intercept 2 can be written in the slope-intercept form as:\n\ny = (-2/3)x + 2\n\nTo find the x-intercept, we set y = 0 and solve for x:\n\n0 = (-2/3)x + 2\nx = -6\n\nTherefore, the x-intercept of the line is x = -6.', token_ids=[1271, 1505, 279, 865, 45994, 1512, 315, 279, 1584, 77933, 311, 279, 1584, 220, 18, 87, 482, 220, 17, 88, 284, 220, 21, 323, 6832, 379, 45994, 1512, 374, 220, 17, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1176, 1505, 279, 31332, 315, 279, 272