Output~2025-04-07 00:38:06.678365: [RequestOutput(request_id=1379, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Recommend a way of studying for a test. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 47706, 264, 1648, 315, 21630, 369, 264, 1296, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here\'s a response that recommends a way of studying for a test:\n\n"To effectively study for a test, I recommend using a combination of active recall and spaced repetition. Here\'s a step-by-step approach you can follow:\n\n1. **Make a study plan**: Start by making a study plan that outlines what you need to study, how much time you have available, and what you want to achieve. Break down your study material into smaller chunks, and prioritize the most important topics.\n2. **Review notes and materials**: Go through your notes and materials, and review the key concepts and information. Summarize the main points in your own words, and try to identify any areas where you\'re struggling.\n3. **Create flashcards**: Create flashcards with key terms or concepts on one side and the definition or explanation on the other. Quiz yourself by covering the answer and trying to recall the information from memory.\n4. **Practice active recall**: Use active recall techniques such as making flashcards, taking practice quizzes, or creating concept maps to test your understanding of the material. The more you practice recalling the information, the more likely you are to remember it.\n5. **Use spaced repetition**: Review the material at increasingly longer intervals to help solidify it in your long-term memory. For example, review the material one day, then again a week later, and finally after a month.\n6. **Get enough sleep**: Make sure you get plenty of sleep before the test. Sleep helps to consolidate memories and improve retention, so aim for 7-9 hours of sleep.\n7. **Stay organized**: Keep all your study materials organized, including your notes, flashcards, and practice quizzes. This will help you stay focused and avoid wasting time searching for information.\n\nBy following these steps, you\'ll be well-prepared for your test and can feel confident in your ability to perform well."', token_ids=[8586, 596, 264, 2077, 430, 40912, 264, 1648, 315, 21630, 369, 264, 1296, 1473, 66220, 13750, 4007, 369, 264, 1296, 11, 358, 7079, 1701, 264, 10824, 315, 4642, 19635, 323, 64928, 54515, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 3094, 14656, 30308, 5603, 499, 649, 1833, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 8238, 264, 4007, 3197, 96618, 5256, 555, 3339, 264, 4007, 3197, 430, 50729, 1148, 499, 1205, 311, 4007, 11, 1268, 1790, 892, 499, 617, 2561, 11, 323, 1148, 499, 1390, 311, 11322, 13, 15996, 1523, 701, 4007, 3769, 1139, 9333, 27855, 11, 323, 63652, 279, 1455, 3062, 13650, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 19997, 8554, 323, 7384, 96618, 6122, 1555, 701, 8554, 323, 7384, 11, 323, 3477, 279, 1401, 19476, 323, 2038, 13, 8279, 5730, 553, 279, 1925, 3585, 304, 701, 1866, 4339, 11, 323, 1456, 311, 10765, 904, 5789, 1405, 499, 2351, 20558, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 4110, 8381, 26076, 96618, 4324, 8381, 26076, 449, 1401, 3878, 477, 19476, 389, 832, 3185, 323, 279, 7419, 477, 16540, 389, 279, 1023, 13, 42248, 6261, 555, 18702, 279, 4320, 323, 4560, 311, 19635, 279, 2038, 505, 5044, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 89592, 4642, 19635, 96618, 5560, 4642, 19635, 12823, 1778, 439, 3339, 8381, 26076, 11, 4737, 6725, 89323, 11, 477, 6968, 7434, 14370, 311, 1296, 701, 8830, 315, 279, 3769, 13, 578, 810, 499, 6725, 89746, 279, 2038, 11, 279, 810, 4461, 499, 527, 311