Output~2025-04-07 00:44:42.745261: [RequestOutput(request_id=1536, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Create a 10-step process for planting a tree. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4324, 264, 220, 605, 30308, 1920, 369, 48114, 264, 5021, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a 10-step process for planting a tree:\n\n**Step 1: Choose the Right Tree**\nSelect a tree species that is suitable for your climate, soil type, and available space. Consider factors such as growth rate, mature size, and maintenance requirements.\n\n**Step 2: Prepare the Site**\nClear the area of any debris, rocks, and weeds. Mark the center of the planting site with a stake and tie a string around it to guide you as you dig.\n\n**Step 3: Dig the Hole**\nDig a hole that is twice as wide and as deep as the root ball of the tree. If your soil is rocky or compacted, you may need to dig a shallower hole and add organic matter to improve drainage.\n\n**Step 4: Remove the Tree from the Container**\nGently remove the tree from its container or burlap, taking care not to damage the roots. If the roots are wrapped in burlap, remove the burlap and any string or wire.\n\n**Step 5: Inspect the Roots**\nInspect the roots for any signs of circling or girdling. If necessary, gently tease out the roots to encourage them to grow outward.\n\n**Step 6: Place the Tree in the Hole**\nPlace the tree in the hole, making sure the root flare (where the trunk flares out at the base of the tree) is level with the soil surface.\n\n**Step 7: Fill the Hole**\nFill the hole with soil, tamping it down gently as you go to prevent air pockets. Make sure the soil level is the same as it was before planting.\n\n**Step 8: Water the Tree**\nWater the tree thoroughly to settle the soil and provide enough moisture to support establishment.\n\n**Step 9: Mulch Around the Tree**\nApply a 2-3 inch layer of organic mulch around the tree, keeping it a few inches away from the trunk. This will help retain moisture and suppress weeds.\n\n**Step 10: Stake the Tree (Optional)**\nIf necessary, stake the tree to prevent wind damage or root disturbance. Use soft ties and remove the stakes after one year to prevent girdling.\n\nBy following these steps, you'll be well on your way to successfully planting a healthy and thriving tree!", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 220, 605, 30308, 1920, 369, 48114, 264, 5021, 1473, 334, 8468, 220, 16, 25, 22991, 279, 10291, 9119, 1035, 3461, 264, 5021, 9606, 430, 374, 14791, 369, 701, 10182, 11, 17614, 955, 11, 323, 2561, 3634, 13, 21829, 9547, 1778, 439, 6650, 4478, 11, 15196, 1404, 11, 323, 13709, 8670, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 17, 25, 32266, 279, 13207, 1035, 14335, 279, 3158, 315, 904, 35098, 11, 23902, 11, 323, 70535, 13, 4488, 279, 4219, 315, 279, 48114, 2816, 449, 264, 18783, 323, 18623, 264, 925, 2212, 433, 311, 8641, 499, 439, 499, 4170, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 18, 25, 39069, 279, 52029, 1035, 38198, 264, 14512, 430, 374, 11157, 439, 7029, 323, 439, 5655, 439, 279, 3789, 5041, 315, 279, 5021, 13, 1442, 701, 17614, 374, 56617, 477, 17251, 291, 11, 499, 1253, 1205, 311, 4170, 264, 4985, 1223, 14512, 323, 923, 17808, 5030, 311, 7417, 58592, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 19, 25, 11016, 279, 9119, 505, 279, 9876, 1035, 38, 4501, 4148, 279, 5021, 505, 1202, 5593, 477, 293, 1103, 391, 11, 4737, 2512, 539, 311, 5674, 279, 20282, 13, 1442, 279, 20282, 527, 20037, 304, 293, 1103, 391, 11, 4148, 279, 293, 1103, 391, 323, 904, 925, 477, 9244, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 20, 25