Output~2025-04-07 00:51:33.944366: [RequestOutput(request_id=1694, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Tell me a horror story in the style of Poe. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 25672, 757, 264, 22169, 3446, 304, 279, 1742, 315, 82695, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='The moon cast its sickly glow over the crumbling mansion, its once-grand facade now shrouded in a thick, eerie mist. The wind howled through the broken windows, its mournful wail echoing through the empty halls like the lamentations of the damned.\n\nI stood before the entrance, my heart heavy with foreboding, as I pushed open the creaking door. The air inside was thick with the scent of decay and rot, and I could feel the weight of centuries of sorrow bearing down upon me.\n\nAs I ventured deeper into the mansion, I stumbled upon a room that seemed frozen in time. The furniture was shrouded in cobwebs, and the walls were adorned with faded portraits of people long since deceased. But it was the centerpiece of the room that caught my attention: a grand, ornate mirror, its surface reflecting the dim light of the moon like a window to the very soul of the damned.\n\nI approached the mirror, my hand reaching out to touch its cold, glassy surface. And as I did, I felt a presence behind me. I spun around, but there was no one there. The wind died down, and an oppressive silence fell over the room.\n\nSuddenly, the mirror began to rattle and shake, its surface distorting like a funhouse mirror. I felt a chill run down my spine as I saw my own reflection staring back at me, its eyes black as coal, its skin gray as the stone that surrounded me.\n\nThe mirror began to speak, its voice like a sighing wind, "You should not have come here. You should not have disturbed the rest of the dead." I tried to turn away, but my feet seemed rooted to the spot.\n\nThe mirror\'s voice grew louder, more menacing, "You will never leave this place. You will never escape the horrors that lurk within these walls." And with that, the mirror shattered, its shards raining down upon me like a hail of glassy tears.\n\nI stumbled backward, tripping over my own feet, as the darkness closed in around me. And when I looked up, I saw the faces of the dead, their eyes black as coal, their skin gray as the stone, staring back at me from the shattered remains of the mirror.\n\nI was consumed by the darkness, trapped in a living nightmare from which I would never awaken. And as the last of my sanity fled, I realized that I was not alone. The dead were all around me, their presence palpable, their whispers echoing in my', token_ids=[791, 18266, 6445, 1202, 14363, 398, 37066, 927, 279, 89417, 52528, 11, 1202, 3131, 72102, 62716, 1457, 559, 583, 9988, 304, 264, 12314, 11, 97383, 8770, 13, 578, 10160, 1268, 839, 1555, 279, 11102, 11276, 11, 1202, 60234, 1285, 289, 607, 94824, 1555, 279, 4384, 52473, 1093, 279, 51472, 811, 315, 279, 68465, 382, 40, 14980, 1603, 279, 20396, 11, 856, 4851, 8987, 449, 2291, 65, 3785, 11, 439, 358, 15753, 1825, 279, 272, 1127, 287, 6134, 13, 578, 3805, 4871, 574, 12314, 449, 279, 41466, 315, 31815, 323, 5868, 11, 323, 358, 1436, 2733, 279, 4785, 315, 24552, 315, 58596, 18534, 1523, 5304, 757, 382, 2170, 358, 99507, 19662, 1139, 279, 52528, 11, 358, 50157, 5304, 264, 3130, 430, 9508, 20268, 304, 892, 13, 578, 14891, 574, 559, 583, 9988, 304, 34928, 89995, 11, 323, 279, 14620, 1051, 84273, 449, 54434, 59234, 315, 1274, 1317, 2533, 43720, 13, 2030, 433, 574